{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01JuWJaPvoRHH2GCmPRDHW7n","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"CoRL 2026 reviewer guidelines review form\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"CoRL 2026 - Instruction for Authors\",\"url\":\"https://www.corl.org/contributions/instruction-for-authors\"},{\"title\":\"CoRL 2026 Conference | OpenReview\",\"url\":\"https://openreview.net/group?id=robot-learning.org%2FCoRL%2F2026%2FConference\"},{\"title\":\"CoRL 2026 - Call for Papers\",\"url\":\"https://www.corl.org/contributions/call-for-papers\"},{\"title\":\"Reviewer Guidelines — CoRL 2023\",\"url\":\"https://www.corl2023.org/reviewer-guidelines\"},{\"title\":\"Robot Learning Foundation\",\"url\":\"https://www.robot-learning.org/\"},{\"title\":\"CoRL 2026\",\"url\":\"https://www.corl.org/\"},{\"title\":\"ICLR 2026 Reviewer Guide\",\"url\":\"https://iclr.cc/Conferences/2026/ReviewerGuide\"},{\"title\":\"CoRL 2024 - Instruction for Reviews\",\"url\":\"https://2024.corl.org/contributions/instruction-for-reviews\"},{\"title\":\"CoRL 2025 Conference | OpenReview\",\"url\":\"https://openreview.net/group?id=robot-learning.org%2FCoRL%2F2025%2FConference\"},{\"title\":\"CVPR 2026 Reviewer Guidelines\",\"url\":\"https://cvpr.thecvf.com/Conferences/2026/ReviewerGuidelinesq\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, I found some relevant information about CoRL 2026, though specific reviewer guidelines and review form details are not fully detailed in the search results. Here's what I found:\n\n## CoRL 2026 Submission and Review Information\n\nAll submissions must include at least one author who agrees to serve as a CoRL reviewer. They are qualified if they have at least one accepted publication at a previous robotics (CoRL/ ICRA/ IROS/ RSS) or learning conference (ICLR/ NeurIPS/ ICML) or equivalent journal.\n\nCoRL aims to have at least two reviewers per paper.\n\n## Review Criteria and Guidelines\n\nWhile the search results don't show the complete CoRL 2026 reviewer guidelines, they do reference guidelines from CoRL 2023 that include:\n\nPapers should address whether the paper addresses a problem in robot learning, whether it applies or improves a learning-based method or learned model, whether the method is evaluated in simulation, on real robots, or both, and whether the CoRL audience would be interested in reading the paper.\n\nCoRL papers are required to include a limitations section, reviewers should treat honestly reported limitations kindly, and obvious shortcomings not reported by the authors should be strongly reflected in scores.\n\nFor the complete and specific CoRL 2026 reviewer guidelines and review form, you may need to visit the official CoRL 2026 website or OpenReview page, as the detailed form information is not fully available in these search results.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f3c89458-961d-4d5e-a388-373831b4983c","uuid":"3d72f053-8dbf-42ca-91f6-b2d0dcd30350","timestamp":"2026-05-15T16:37:00.570Z","tool_use_result":{"query":"CoRL 2026 reviewer guidelines review form","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_01XY1MhEbBFGfJcw4PXLifvf","content":[{"title":"CoRL 2026 - Instruction for Authors","url":"https://www.corl.org/contributions/instruction-for-authors"},{"title":"CoRL 2026 Conference | OpenReview","url":"https://openreview.net/group?id=robot-learning.org%2FCoRL%2F2026%2FConference"},{"title":"CoRL 2026 - Call for Papers","url":"https://www.corl.org/contributions/call-for-papers"},{"title":"Reviewer Guidelines — CoRL 2023","url":"https://www.corl2023.org/reviewer-guidelines"},{"title":"Robot Learning Foundation","url":"https://www.robot-learning.org/"},{"title":"CoRL 2026","url":"https://www.corl.org/"},{"title":"ICLR 2026 Reviewer Guide","url":"https://iclr.cc/Conferences/2026/ReviewerGuide"},{"title":"CoRL 2024 - Instruction for Reviews","url":"https://2024.corl.org/contributions/instruction-for-reviews"},{"title":"CoRL 2025 Conference | OpenReview","url":"https://openreview.net/group?id=robot-learning.org%2FCoRL%2F2025%2FConference"},{"title":"CVPR 2026 Reviewer Guidelines","url":"https://cvpr.thecvf.com/Conferences/2026/ReviewerGuidelinesq"}]},"Based on the search results, I found some relevant information about CoRL 2026, though specific reviewer guidelines and review form details are not fully detailed in the search results. Here's what I found:\n\n## CoRL 2026 Submission and Review Information\n\nAll submissions must include at least one author who agrees to serve as a CoRL reviewer. They are qualified if they have at least one accepted publication at a previous robotics (CoRL/ ICRA/ IROS/ RSS) or learning conference (ICLR/ NeurIPS/ ICML) or equivalent journal.\n\nCoRL aims to have at least two reviewers per paper.\n\n## Review Criteria and Guidelines\n\nWhile the search results don't show the complete CoRL 2026 reviewer guidelines, they do reference guidelines from CoRL 2023 that include:\n\nPapers should address whether the paper addresses a problem in robot learning, whether it applies or improves a learning-based method or learned model, whether the method is evaluated in simulation, on real robots, or both, and whether the CoRL audience would be interested in reading the paper.\n\nCoRL papers are required to include a limitations section, reviewers should treat honestly reported limitations kindly, and obvious shortcomings not reported by the authors should be strongly reflected in scores.\n\nFor the complete and specific CoRL 2026 reviewer guidelines and review form, you may need to visit the official CoRL 2026 website or OpenReview page, as the detailed form information is not fully available in these search results."],"durationSeconds":5.93467193}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01DxKshGjQN97B2hE2RiwCjV","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"CoRL 2025 2024 reviewer guidelines scoring rubric acceptance rate\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"CORL 2025 Statistics - Paper Copilot\",\"url\":\"https://papercopilot.com/statistics/corl-statistics/corl-2025-statistics/\"},{\"title\":\"CoRL 2025 Accepted Paper List - Paper Copilot\",\"url\":\"https://papercopilot.com/paper-list/corl-paper-list/corl-2025-paper-list/\"},{\"title\":\"CoRL Statistics - Paper Copilot\",\"url\":\"https://papercopilot.com/statistics/corl-statistics/\"},{\"title\":\"About Our Ratings & Reviews [2025]\",\"url\":\"https://educationdata.org/about-our-ratings-reviews\"},{\"title\":\"CoRL 2025 Conference | OpenReview\",\"url\":\"https://openreview.net/group?id=robot-learning.org%2FCoRL%2F2025%2FConference\"},{\"title\":\"Reviewer Guidelines — CoRL 2023\",\"url\":\"https://www.corl2023.org/reviewer-guidelines\"},{\"title\":\"CoRL 2026 - Instruction for Authors\",\"url\":\"https://www.corl.org/contributions/instruction-for-authors\"},{\"title\":\"CoRL 2024 Accepted Paper List - Paper Copilot\",\"url\":\"https://papercopilot.com/paper-list/corl-paper-list/corl-2024-paper-list/\"},{\"title\":\"CoRL 2025 Demos | OpenReview\",\"url\":\"https://openreview.net/group?id=robot-learning.org%2FCoRL%2F2025%2FDemos\"},{\"title\":\"2025 Reviewer Guidelines\",\"url\":\"https://neurips.cc/Conferences/2025/ReviewerGuidelines\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, I found some relevant information about CoRL review guidelines, though comprehensive scoring rubric details for CoRL 2025 specifically were not fully available. Here's what I found:\n\n## Reviewer Guidelines\n\nThe CoRL review process is about three months long, submission-to-notification, including the discussion period. CoRL papers are required to include a limitations section, and reviewers should treat honestly reported limitations kindly and with high appreciation, while obvious shortcomings not reported by the authors should be pointed out extensively and strongly reflected in scores.\n\nReviewers are instructed to be constructive and concrete, courteous and respectful, starting with positive aspects and suggesting improvements, while making reviews as informative and substantiated as possible.\n\n## Process Details\n\nThe conference aims to have at least two reviewers per paper.\n\n## Acceptance Rate\n\nUnfortunately, the search results did not contain specific information about the CoRL 2025 acceptance rate or a detailed scoring rubric. The search results reference CoRL 2023 reviewer guidelines and general CoRL infrastructure pages, but the specific scoring rubric and current acceptance rate statistics are not included in these results. You may find more detailed information by checking the OpenReview page for CoRL 2025 directly or the official CoRL website.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f3c89458-961d-4d5e-a388-373831b4983c","uuid":"b0517fb3-d2ac-49fc-b6f9-82c22948365b","timestamp":"2026-05-15T16:37:01.366Z","tool_use_result":{"query":"CoRL 2025 2024 reviewer guidelines scoring rubric acceptance rate","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_01DXdE7RpuFPMEGSzPzreCD4","content":[{"title":"CORL 2025 Statistics - Paper Copilot","url":"https://papercopilot.com/statistics/corl-statistics/corl-2025-statistics/"},{"title":"CoRL 2025 Accepted Paper List - Paper Copilot","url":"https://papercopilot.com/paper-list/corl-paper-list/corl-2025-paper-list/"},{"title":"CoRL Statistics - Paper Copilot","url":"https://papercopilot.com/statistics/corl-statistics/"},{"title":"About Our Ratings & Reviews [2025]","url":"https://educationdata.org/about-our-ratings-reviews"},{"title":"CoRL 2025 Conference | OpenReview","url":"https://openreview.net/group?id=robot-learning.org%2FCoRL%2F2025%2FConference"},{"title":"Reviewer Guidelines — CoRL 2023","url":"https://www.corl2023.org/reviewer-guidelines"},{"title":"CoRL 2026 - Instruction for Authors","url":"https://www.corl.org/contributions/instruction-for-authors"},{"title":"CoRL 2024 Accepted Paper List - Paper Copilot","url":"https://papercopilot.com/paper-list/corl-paper-list/corl-2024-paper-list/"},{"title":"CoRL 2025 Demos | OpenReview","url":"https://openreview.net/group?id=robot-learning.org%2FCoRL%2F2025%2FDemos"},{"title":"2025 Reviewer Guidelines","url":"https://neurips.cc/Conferences/2025/ReviewerGuidelines"}]},"Based on the search results, I found some relevant information about CoRL review guidelines, though comprehensive scoring rubric details for CoRL 2025 specifically were not fully available. Here's what I found:\n\n## Reviewer Guidelines\n\nThe CoRL review process is about three months long, submission-to-notification, including the discussion period. CoRL papers are required to include a limitations section, and reviewers should treat honestly reported limitations kindly and with high appreciation, while obvious shortcomings not reported by the authors should be pointed out extensively and strongly reflected in scores.\n\nReviewers are instructed to be constructive and concrete, courteous and respectful, starting with positive aspects and suggesting improvements, while making reviews as informative and substantiated as possible.\n\n## Process Details\n\nThe conference aims to have at least two reviewers per paper.\n\n## Acceptance Rate\n\nUnfortunately, the search results did not contain specific information about the CoRL 2025 acceptance rate or a detailed scoring rubric. The search results reference CoRL 2023 reviewer guidelines and general CoRL infrastructure pages, but the specific scoring rubric and current acceptance rate statistics are not included in these results. You may find more detailed information by checking the OpenReview page for CoRL 2025 directly or the official CoRL website."],"durationSeconds":6.143169001999999}}
