"CoRL 2024 - Speakers\",\"url\":\"https://2024.corl.org/program/speakers\"},{\"title\":\"CoRL 2024 - Papers XX\",\"url\":\"https://2024.corl.org/program/papers-xx\"},{\"title\":\"CoRL 2024\",\"url\":\"https://2024.corl.org/\"},{\"title\":\"CoRL 2024 - Demos\",\"url\":\"https://2024.corl.org/program/demos\"}]\n\nLet me search more specifically for the review form details with rating definitions.\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"CoRL 2024 Accepted Paper List - Paper Copilot\",\"url\":\"https://papercopilot.com/paper-list/corl-paper-list/corl-2024-paper-list/\"}]\n\nBased on my web search results, I found the CoRL 2024 Instruction for Reviews page, but the search results show only partial content. The specific rating scale details (1-10 scale) appear to be on that page but weren't fully captured in the search results.\n\nFrom what I found, submissions for CoRL 2024 were evaluated based on the significance and novelty of the results, either theoretical or empirical, with results judged on the degree to which they have been objectively established and/or their potential for scientific and technological impact, as well as their relevance to robotic learning.\n\nThe search results also indicate that papers are ordered based on review rating and review confidence, and that reviewers provide numerical scores. However, the specific 1-10 rating scale definition and detailed instructions that would be in the full review form were not completely captured in the search results I retrieved.\n\nTo see the complete review form instructions including the specific rating scale definitions, I recommend visiting the official CoRL 2024 website directly at https://2024.corl.org/contributions/instruction-for-reviews or accessing the OpenReview page for CoRL 2024 where reviewers would have submitted their evaluations.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f3c89458-961d-4d5e-a388-373831b498