://www.corl2023.org/\"},{\"title\":\"CoRL 2023 Conference | OpenReview\",\"url\":\"https://openreview.net/group?id=robot-learning.org%2FCoRL%2F2023%2FConference\"},{\"title\":\"Papers — CoRL 2023\",\"url\":\"https://www.corl2023.org/papers\"},{\"title\":\"Conference on Robot Learning (CoRL) 2023 Note Seungchan Kim (CMU)\",\"url\":\"https://seungchan-kim.github.io/notes/CoRL_2023_Note.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"Instructions for Presentations — CoRL 2023\",\"url\":\"https://www.corl2023.org/instructions-for-presentations\"},{\"title\":\"My Paper Reviewing Load\",\"url\":\"https://danieltakeshi.github.io/2022/04/23/paper-reviewing-load/\"}]\n\nBased on my search attempts, I've accessed the CoRL 2023 Reviewer Guidelines page multiple times, but the full rating scale definitions don't appear in the publicly available excerpts from the web search results. The guidelines page discusses the review process and evaluation criteria (originality, quality, clarity, significance, relevance, and limitations), but the specific \"1-10 overall score\" rating scale definitions that you're looking for aren't showing up in the search results.\n\nThe web search results do show that CoRL 2023 used numeric scores (with papers receiving ratings around 3, 4, 5 based on the Paper Copilot statistics), but the detailed descriptions for each point on a 1-10 scale aren't included in the accessible portions of the CoRL 2023 website captured by the search engine.\n\nTo find the complete rating scale with descriptions, you may need to:\n1. Visit the full CoRL 2023 Reviewer Guidelines page directly at https://www.corl2023.org/reviewer-guidelines\n2. Check the OpenReview submission form at https://openreview.net/group?id=robot-learning.org%2FCoRL%2F2023%2FConference\n3. Look for any PDF documentation or reviewer instruction materials that were provided to reviewers during the submission period\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"paren