tions a rebuttal phase for papers that don't receive all rejection ratings.\n\nBased on the search results, here's what I found about CoRL's review system on OpenReview:\n\nPapers that receive all reviews in the \"reject\" range in the initial round will not proceed to the rebuttal phase, which implies there are rating categories beyond \"reject.\" The search results show that the main review part of the review form asks for an evaluation of the originality, quality, clarity, significance, relevance and limitations of this work.\n\nHowever, the search results don't provide the complete rating scale with the exact labels like \"strong accept,\" \"accept,\" \"reject\" and their corresponding numerical values that you're asking about. To get the precise overall rating scale used for CoRL reviews on OpenReview, you may need to visit the OpenReview submission portal directly or check the detailed review form instructions on the specific CoRL conference year's page.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f3c89458-961d-4d5e-a388-373831b4983c","uuid":"8531a7e3-1367-4e25-841c-c4a4a2ec20b1","timestamp":"2026-05-15T16:38:01.533Z","tool_use_result":{"query":"CoRL openreview review \"overall rating\" \"strong accept\" \"accept\" \"reject\" scale robot learning","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_0123RuFenX6qJiMcXeWCHqmF","content":[{"title":"Reviewer Guidelines — CoRL 2023","url":"https://www.corl2023.org/reviewer-guidelines"},{"title":"CoRL | OpenReview","url":"https://openreview.net/group?id=robot-learning.org%2FCoRL"},{"title":"CoRL 2026 - Instruction for Authors","url":"https://www.corl.org/contributions/instruction-for-authors"},{"title":"CoRL 2024 - Instruction for Reviews","url":"https://2024.corl.org/contributions/instruction-for-reviews"},{"title":"CoRL 2026 Conference | OpenReview","url":"https://openreview.net/group?id=robot-learning.org%2FCoRL%2F2026%2FConf