 Perturbation Correction: FTM, FLA\n- Parameter-Efficient Adaptation: LoRA, LoRA-SP, QLoRA, MoIRA, CORAL\n- Perturbation Diagnosis: SAFE, OpenVLA probing, pi0.5 feature steering\n\n**Key results**:\n- 71.4% overall, +17.8% over frozen, +6.0% over universal LoRA\n- 64.5% of VLA-GSE gain at 5.3% of parameters (but different backbone caveat)\n- Cross-backbone SmolVLA replicates qualitative pattern (+5.6%)\n- Routing gains asymmetric: Visual +8.7%, Spatial +1.1%, Physical +5.2%\n- Layer placement crossed-peak pattern: V→early, S→mid, P→late\n\n## Your Task\nProvide a detailed review focused on **Novelty** and **Related Work**. Structure your review as:\n\n### 1. Summary (2-3 sentences)\n\n### 2. Novelty Assessment (detailed)\n- How novel is the core observation (activations encode perturbation type)?\n- How novel is the routing architecture itself?\n- How novel is the perturbation taxonomy (Visual/Spatial/Physical)?\n- Is \"closing the diagnose-correct loop\" genuinely new or incremental combination?\n\n### 3. Related Work Gaps\n- Are there missing references or comparisons?\n- Is the positioning relative to existing work fair and accurate?\n- Consider: MoE routing literature, domain adaptation, test-time adaptation, robustness literature beyond VLAs\n\n### 4. Strengths (bulleted, focus on originality and positioning)\n\n### 5. Weaknesses (bulleted, focus on novelty limitations and related work gaps)\n\n### 6. Questions for Authors\n\n### 7. Scores\n- Novelty (1-4): How original is this work?\n- Related Work Coverage (1-4): How complete is the literature survey?\n- Significance (1-4): Will this influence future work?\n- Overall Rating (1-10, CoRL scale)\n- Confidence (1-5)\n\nBe rigorous but fair. Pay special attention to:\n- Whether the \"frozen activations encode perturbation type\" finding is truly novel given SAFE, OpenVLA probing studies, and feature steering on pi0.5 (all cited by the paper itself)\n- Whether \"routing LoRA experts by perturbation type\" is a sufficiently novel idea versus standard MoE/LoRA routing\n- Whether the paper adequately distinguishes from MoIRA/CORAL (task routing vs perturbation routing) — is this distinction meaningful enough?\n- The framing of \"orthogonal design dimension\" — is this overstatement?\n- Whether the mechanistic analysis (layer placement, spatial limitation) constitutes genuine novelty\n- Missing comparisons to test-time adaptation methods, domain generalization, or other robustness paradigms\n- The reference list is quite short (9 references) — is this adequate?\n"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01SCpZUDUWJBkc4eqtEYBXAg","session_id":"f3c89458-961d-4d5e-a388-373831b4983c","uuid":"48a69e4e-c07d-46e5-b411-584c932bdeb4","timestamp":"2026-05-15T16:39:00.252Z"}
