{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01MGwHzghGqyDMtZcRDvSPcw","type":"tool_result","content":"1\tnarrative_guidance: 'Routing by perturbation type yields clear but moderate gains,\n2\t  strongest on Visual and Physical where perturbations disrupt localized processing\n3\t  stages. Spatial expert underperforms due to layout/distractor perturbations requiring\n4\t  whole-trajectory reasoning beyond single-step LoRA correction. Universal LoRA is\n5\t  a surprisingly strong baseline (~65%) from mixed-training cross-type robustness,\n6\t  narrowing the routing advantage. Frame Meta-Brain as parameter-efficient complement\n7\t  to capacity routing: ~65% of VLA-GSE absolute gain at 5% parameters. Ablation ladder\n8\t  Frozen < Universal < Meta-Brain < Oracle is clean and statistically significant.\n9\t  Add mechanistic analysis section explaining per-type routing benefit asymmetry —\n10\t  turns partial spatial result into insight rather than weakness. Consider additional\n11\t  experiment combining Meta-Brain + universal LoRA residual to show routing is additive\n12\t  to uniform adaptation.\n13\t\n14\t  '\n15\timagined_experiments:\n16\t- name: LoRA Expert Training — Specialized vs Universal\n17\t  plan_id: plan_002\n18\t  description: 'Train 4 rank-16 LoRA adapters on frozen pi0: LoRA-V (visual data),\n19\t    LoRA-S (spatial data), LoRA-P (physical data), Universal (mixed all-type data).\n20\t    Evaluate each on all 7 perturbation types to obtain the cross-type performance\n21\t    matrix.\n22\t\n23\t    '\n24\t  expected_results:\n25\t    lora_v_visual_avg: 78.3\n26\t    lora_v_camera: 75.2\n27\t    lora_v_light: 82.0\n28\t    lora_v_background: 78.4\n29\t    lora_v_noise: 77.6\n30\t    lora_v_spatial_avg: 54.0\n31\t    lora_v_physical: 50.6\n32\t    lora_s_spatial_avg: 68.0\n33\t    lora_s_distractor: 69.4\n34\t    lora_s_layout: 66.6\n35\t    lora_s_visual_avg: 46.9\n36\t    lora_s_physical: 49.2\n37\t    lora_p_physical: 78.0\n38\t    lora_p_visual_avg: 47.9\n39\t    lora_p_spatial_avg: 53.7\n40\t    universal_overall: 65.4\n41\t    universal_visual_avg: 65.35\n42\t    universal_spatial_avg: 63.7\n43\t    universal_physical: 69.0\n44\t    specialization_delta_visual: 12.95\n45\t    specialization_delta_spatial: 4.3\n46\t    specialization_delta_physical: 9.0\n47\t    specialization_delta_max: 12.95\n48\t  result_rationale: 'Visual expert (LoRA-V) shows the strongest specialization (+13%\n49\t    over universal on visual types) because visual perturbations (camera/light/background/noise)\n50\t    corrupt early PaliGemma representations in a consistent, localized manner — rank-16\n51\t    LoRA can learn a compact correction to these early-layer distortions. Physical\n52\t    expert (LoRA-P) shows strong but smaller specialization (+9%) because robot perturbations\n53\t    (changed dynamics/mass) affect action-space outputs which are more distributed\n54\t    across layers. Spatial expert (LoRA-S) shows weak specialization (+4.3%) because\n55\t    layout and distractor perturbations fundamentally change the required trajectory\n56\t    — not just a representational shift but a different action sequence — and single-step\n57\t    LoRA correction at the representation level cannot replan a trajectory. Cross-type\n58\t    performance degrades sharply (below frozen baseline) because each specialized\n59\t    expert learns type-specific correction biases that actively harm representations\n60\t    when applied to the wrong perturbation type. Universal LoRA at 65.4% is stronger\n61\t    than expected because mixed training provides partial cross-type robustness —\n62\t    the LoRA learns an average correction that modestly helps all types without hurting\n63\t    any.\n64\t\n65\t    '\n66\t  tables:\n67\t  - name: Cross-Type Expert Performance Matrix (success rate %)\n68\t    header:\n69\t    - Method\n70\t    - camera\n71\t    - light\n72\t    - background\n73\t    - noise\n74\t    - distractor\n75\t    - layout\n76\t    - robot\n77\t    - Overall\n78\t    rows:\n79\t    - - Frozen pi0\n80\t      - 47.6\n81\t      - 56.2\n82\t      - 51.8\n83\t      - 49.4\n84\t      - 58.6\n85\t      - 57.8\n86\t      - 53.8\n87\t      - 53.6\n88\t    - - LoRA-V\n89\t      - 75.2\n90\t      - 82.0\n91\t      - 78.4\n92\t      - 77.6\n93\t      - 54.2\n94\t      - 53.8\n95\t      - 50.6\n96\t      - 67.4\n97\t    - - LoRA-S\n98\t      - 44.2\n99\t      - 50.4\n100\t      - 47.8\n101\t      - 45.0\n102\t      - 69.4\n103\t      - 66.6\n104\t      - 49.2\n105\t      - 53.2\n106\t    - - LoRA-P\n107\t      - 45.6\n108\t      - 51.2\n109\t      - 48.4\n110\t      - 46.2\n111\t      - 54.0\n112\t      - 53.4\n113\t      - 78.0\n114\t      - 53.8\n115\t    - - Universal\n116\t      - 62.8\n117\t      - 69.4\n118\t      - 66.2\n119\t      - 63.0\n120\t      - 64.8\n121\t      - 62.6\n122\t      - 69.0\n123\t      - 65.4\n124\t  - name: Specialization Delta (expert own-type minus universal same-type)\n125\t    header:\n126\t    - Coarse Type\n127\t    - Expert Own-Type\n128\t    - Universal Same-Type\n129\t    - Delta\n130\t    rows:\n131\t    - - Visual\n132\t      - 78.3\n133\t      - 65.35\n134\t      - 12.95\n135\t    - - Spatial\n136\t      - 68.0\n137\t      - 63.7\n138\t      - 4.3\n139\t    - - Physical\n140\t      - 78.0\n141\t      - 69.0\n142\t      - 9.0\n143\t  figures_description:\n144\t  - 'Heatmap (4 experts × 7 perturbation types) with success rates. Strong diagonal\n145\t    blocks visible for LoRA-V (4 visual columns bright) and LoRA-P (robot column bright).\n146\t    LoRA-S shows only moderate brightness on distractor/layout. Universal row uniformly\n147\t    mid-tone. Off-diagonal cells for specialized experts are dark (below frozen baseline),\n148\t    visually demonstrating the cost of mismatched routing.\n149\t\n150\t    '\n151\t  - 'Grouped bar chart: 3 coarse types on x-axis, bars for [Frozen, Universal, Specialized\n152\t    Expert]. Visual group shows large gap between universal and LoRA-V. Physical group\n153\t    shows moderate gap. Spatial group shows minimal gap. Frozen baseline as dashed\n154\t    horizontal line per group.\n155\t\n156\t    '\n157\t  analysis: 'The cross-type matrix is the foundational evidence for why routing matters:\n158\t    correct expert helps significantly (+9 to +13% over universal), wrong expert hurts\n159\t    severely (below frozen). This asymmetry means random or poor routing can be worse\n160\t    than no routing at all, motivating the need for accurate PAR classification. The\n161\t    weak spatial specialization is interpretable: layout and distractor perturbations\n162\t    change the goal-relevant spatial configuration, requiring trajectory-level replanning\n163\t    that a single-step representation correction cannot provide. This is a fundamental\n164\t    limitation of the LoRA-based approach for spatial perturbations, not a routing\n165\t    failure. The universal LoRA''s surprising strength (65.4%) sets a high bar for\n166\t    Meta-Brain — the routing system must do substantially better to justify 3× the\n167\t    parameters.\n168\t\n169\t    '\n170\t- name: Meta-Brain Assembly — PAR Router + LoRA Bank\n171\t  plan_id: plan_003\n172\t  description: 'Assemble PAR router (PaliGemma layer 6, 2-layer MLP, initialized from\n173\t    Phase 0 weights) with 3 LoRA experts. Soft routing: h_corrected = h_frozen + Σ_k\n174\t    p(type_k) · LoRA_k(h_frozen). End-to-end routing fine-tuning with frozen LoRA\n175\t    parameters (only tune PAR weights). Evaluate on full LIBERO-Plus benchmark.\n176\t\n177\t    '\n178\t  expected_results:\n179\t    libero_plus_overall: 71.4\n180\t    per_type_camera: 71.0\n181\t    per_type_light: 77.6\n182\t    per_type_background: 74.4\n183\t    per_type_noise: 73.0\n184\t    per_type_distractor: 65.2\n185\t    per_type_layout: 64.4\n186\t    per_type_robot: 74.2\n187\t    visual_avg: 74.0\n188\t    spatial_avg: 64.8\n189\t    physical: 74.2\n190\t    gain_over_frozen: 17.8\n191\t    gain_over_universal: 6.0\n192\t    routing_diag_visual: 0.82\n193\t    routing_diag_spatial: 0.68\n194\t    routing_diag_physical: 0.8\n195\t    routing_diagonality_mean: 0.77\n196\t    hard_assignment_accuracy: 89.0\n197\t  result_rationale: 'Soft routing dilutes the correction signal compared to hard (oracle)\n198\t    routing, costing ~4% overall. The dilution is uniform across types (3-5% per type)\n199\t    because even a small weight on the wrong expert introduces harmful correction\n200\t    biases. Spatial routing diagonality is lowest (0.68) because layout/distractor\n201\t    perturbations share visual features with camera/background changes at layer 6\n202\t    — the PAR router''s operating point. Despite this, Meta-Brain still improves over\n203\t    universal on spatial (+1.1%) because even imperfect soft routing toward LoRA-S\n204\t    is better than no type awareness. Visual gain (+8.65% over universal) is large\n205\t    because high routing confidence (0.82) allows LoRA-V to dominate the correction.\n206\t    Physical gain (+5.2%) is moderate due to good routing (0.80) but more distributed\n207\t    perturbation effects. Hard assignment accuracy (89%) is lower than Phase 0 classification\n208\t    (99.3%) because the router is fine-tuned for task success, not classification\n209\t    accuracy — it learns to soften assignments when mixing provides marginal task\n210\t    benefit.\n211\t\n212\t    '\n213\t  tables:\n214\t  - name: Meta-Brain Per-Perturbation Success Rate (%)\n215\t    header:\n216\t    - Perturbation\n217\t    - Frozen\n218\t    - Universal\n219\t    - Meta-Brain\n220\t    - Gain over Universal\n221\t    rows:\n222\t    - - camera\n223\t      - 47.6\n224\t      - 62.8\n225\t      - 71.0\n226\t      - 8.2\n227\t    - - light\n228\t      - 56.2\n229\t      - 69.4\n230\t      - 77.6\n231\t      - 8.2\n232\t    - - background\n233\t      - 51.8\n234\t      - 66.2\n235\t      - 74.4\n236\t      - 8.2\n237\t    - - noise\n238\t      - 49.4\n239\t      - 63.0\n240\t      - 73.0\n241\t      - 10.0\n242\t    - - distractor\n243\t      - 58.6\n244\t      - 64.8\n245\t      - 65.2\n246\t      - 0.4\n247\t    - - layout\n248\t      - 57.8\n249\t      - 62.6\n250\t      - 64.4\n251\t      - 1.8\n252\t    - - robot\n253\t      - 53.8\n254\t      - 69.0\n255\t      - 74.2\n256\t      - 5.2\n257\t    - - Overall\n258\t      - 53.6\n259\t      - 65.4\n260\t      - 71.4\n261\t      - 6.0\n262\t  - name: PAR Soft Routing Weight Matrix (mean weights per true type)\n263\t    header:\n264\t    - True Type\n265\t    - P(LoRA-V)\n266\t    - P(LoRA-S)\n267\t    - P(LoRA-P)\n268\t    rows:\n269\t    - - Visual\n270\t      - 0.82\n271\t      - 0.06\n272\t      - 0.12\n273\t    - - Spatial\n274\t      - 0.2\n275\t      - 0.68\n276\t      - 0.12\n277\t    - - Physical\n278\t      - 0.12\n279\t      - 0.08\n280\t      - 0.8\n281\t  figures_description:\n282\t  - 'Routing weight heatmap (3×3): rows = true perturbation type, columns = routing\n283\t    weight to expert. Near-diagonal pattern visible but imperfect. Visual and Physical\n284\t    rows show strong diagonal dominance (0.82, 0.80). Spatial row is more diffuse\n285\t    (0.68 diagonal, 0.20 leak to Visual). Annotated with actual weight values in each\n286\t    cell.\n287\t\n288\t    '\n289\t  - 'Per-type success rate bar chart: 7 perturbation types on x-axis, grouped bars\n290\t    for Frozen/Universal/Meta-Brain. Clear visual separation on camera/light/background/noise\n291\t    (Meta-Brain >> Universal >> Frozen). Minimal separation on distractor/layout.\n292\t    Moderate separation on robot.\n293\t\n294\t    '\n295\t  analysis: 'Meta-Brain achieves the target ordering (Meta-Brain > Universal > Frozen\n296\t    on all 7 types) but the margin varies dramatically: +8-10% on visual types, +5%\n297\t    on physical, only +0.4-1.8% on spatial. This asymmetry is mechanistically interpretable:\n298\t    visual perturbations corrupt the representation in a way that a type-specific\n299\t    LoRA can precisely invert, while spatial perturbations require policy-level replanning\n300\t    beyond representation correction. The routing weight analysis reveals the PAR\n301\t    router appropriately lacks confidence on spatial inputs (diag 0.68), which limits\n302\t    both the benefit and the harm of routing on these types. The end-to-end routing\n303\t    fine-tuning shifts the router from pure classification toward task-success optimization,\n304\t    explaining the gap between Phase 0 accuracy (99.3%) and deployed routing accuracy\n305\t    (~89%).\n306\t\n307\t    '\n308\t- name: Oracle Routing — Upper Bound for Routing Quality\n309\t  plan_id: plan_004\n310\t  description: 'Replace PAR soft router with ground-truth perturbation type labels\n311\t    (hard 1-hot routing to the correct expert). Same LoRA experts from plan_002. Measures\n312\t    the ceiling for routing quality and quantifies PAR''s gap to perfect routing.\n313\t\n314\t    '\n315\t  expected_results:\n316\t    oracle_overall: 75.3\n317\t    oracle_camera: 75.2\n318\t    oracle_light: 82.0\n319\t    oracle_background: 78.4\n320\t    oracle_noise: 77.6\n321\t    oracle_distractor: 69.4\n322\t    oracle_layout: 66.6\n323\t    oracle_robot: 78.0\n324\t    oracle_par_gap_overall: 3.9\n325\t    oracle_par_gap_visual: 4.3\n326\t    oracle_par_gap_spatial: 3.8\n327\t    oracle_par_gap_physical: 3.8\n328\t  result_rationale: 'Oracle routing eliminates soft-routing dilution entirely — each\n329\t    perturbation type receives 100% correction from its matched expert, with zero\n330\t    contamination from mismatched experts. The 3.9% overall gap from Meta-Brain to\n331\t    oracle quantifies the cost of learned soft routing versus perfect hard routing.\n332\t    This gap arises from two sources: (1) non-zero weight on wrong experts injects\n333\t    harmful correction biases (~60% of the gap), and (2) the router''s lower confidence\n334\t    on spatial perturbations causes LoRA-S to be under-weighted even on true spatial\n335\t    inputs (~40% of the gap). The gap is moderate (not catastrophic), indicating PAR\n336\t    routing is functional but not near-perfect. Closing this gap further would require\n337\t    either better features for spatial classification at layer 6, or a hybrid routing\n338\t    scheme that uses hard routing when confidence is high and universal fallback when\n339\t    confidence is low. Note that oracle performance (75.3%) still trails VLA-GSE (81.2%)\n340\t    by 5.9%, confirming that the performance ceiling is set by pi0 backbone capacity\n341\t    and LoRA rank, not routing quality.\n342\t\n343\t    '\n344\t  tables:\n345\t  - name: Oracle vs PAR Per-Type Gap (%)\n346\t    header:\n347\t    - Perturbation\n348\t    - Oracle\n349\t    - Meta-Brain (PAR)\n350\t    - Gap\n351\t    rows:\n352\t    - - camera\n353\t      - 75.2\n354\t      - 71.0\n355\t      - 4.2\n356\t    - - light\n357\t      - 82.0\n358\t      - 77.6\n359\t      - 4.4\n360\t    - - background\n361\t      - 78.4\n362\t      - 74.4\n363\t      - 4.0\n364\t    - - noise\n365\t      - 77.6\n366\t      - 73.0\n367\t      - 4.6\n368\t    - - distractor\n369\t      - 69.4\n370\t      - 65.2\n371\t      - 4.2\n372\t    - - layout\n373\t      - 66.6\n374\t      - 64.4\n375\t      - 2.2\n376\t    - - robot\n377\t      - 78.0\n378\t      - 74.2\n379\t      - 3.8\n380\t    - - Overall\n381\t      - 75.3\n382\t      - 71.4\n383\t      - 3.9\n384\t  figures_description:\n385\t  - 'Paired bar chart: for each perturbation type, side-by-side bars for Oracle (blue)\n386\t    and Meta-Brain PAR (orange) with the gap annotated above. Layout has the smallest\n387\t    gap (2.2%) because LoRA-S is already weak regardless of routing. Noise has the\n388\t    largest gap (4.6%) because sensor noise is hardest for the router to confidently\n389\t    classify.\n390\t\n391\t    '\n392\t  analysis: 'The oracle-PAR gap of 3.9% is in the moderate range — large enough to\n393\t    matter for absolute performance but not large enough to invalidate the routing\n394\t    approach. The implication for Claim 2 is important: even with perfect routing,\n395\t    the gain over universal LoRA would be 75.3 - 65.4 = 9.9%, only ~64% more than\n396\t    Meta-Brain''s 6.0%. This means routing quality accounts for ~40% of the potential\n397\t    routing benefit left on the table. For the paper, frame this as: \"PAR captures\n398\t    ~60% of the theoretically available routing benefit, with the remaining gap attributable\n399\t    to soft-routing dilution and spatial ambiguity.\" The gap also establishes headroom\n400\t    for future router improvements (e.g., confidence-gated hard routing).\n401\t\n402\t    '\n403\t- name: Ablation Ladder — Frozen → Universal → Meta-Brain → Oracle\n404\t  plan_id: plan_005\n405\t  description: 'Systematic 5-seed comparison on full LIBERO-Plus: Frozen pi0, Universal\n406\t    LoRA (rank 16, ~2M), Meta-Brain (PAR + 3 LoRA, ~6M), Oracle routing (ground-truth\n407\t    type). Report overall and per-perturbation breakdown with statistical significance.\n408\t    Core evidence for Claim 2.\n409\t\n410\t    '\n411\t  expected_results:\n412\t    frozen_mean: 53.6\n413\t    frozen_std: 1.8\n414\t    universal_mean: 65.4\n415\t    universal_std: 2.1\n416\t    meta_brain_mean: 71.4\n417\t    meta_brain_std: 2.4\n418\t    oracle_mean: 75.3\n419\t    oracle_std: 1.9\n420\t    gain_frozen_to_universal: 11.8\n421\t    gain_universal_to_meta_brain: 6.0\n422\t    gain_meta_brain_to_oracle: 3.9\n423\t    pvalue_universal_gt_frozen: 0.0003\n424\t    pvalue_meta_brain_gt_universal: 0.008\n425\t    pvalue_oracle_gt_meta_brain: 0.021\n426\t    meta_brain_gain_over_frozen: 17.8\n427\t  result_rationale: 'The ablation ladder shows a clean monotonic ordering (Frozen\n428\t    < Universal < Meta-Brain < Oracle) with all adjacent pairs statistically significant\n429\t    at p < 0.05. Step sizes decrease going up the ladder: +11.8 (baseline adaptation),\n430\t    +6.0 (routing benefit), +3.9 (routing quality gap). The largest step is Frozen\n431\t    → Universal, confirming that simply adding LoRA adaptation captures most of the\n432\t    low-hanging fruit. The Universal → Meta-Brain step (+6.0%) is the headline number\n433\t    for Claim 2 — routing by perturbation type provides meaningful additional benefit\n434\t    beyond uniform adaptation, but the advantage is moderate (not dominant). The diminishing\n435\t    step sizes reflect a fundamental pattern: each successive refinement addresses\n436\t    a smaller remaining error surface. Standard deviations are 1.8-2.4%, typical for\n437\t    LIBERO-Plus with per-seed task ordering variance. Meta-Brain''s higher std (2.4%)\n438\t    reflects routing sensitivity to seed-specific perturbation distributions.\n439\t\n440\t    '\n441\t  tables:\n442\t  - name: Ablation Ladder — Overall Success Rate (%, 5 seeds)\n443\t    header:\n444\t    - Method\n445\t    - Params\n446\t    - Mean\n447\t    - Std\n448\t    - 95% CI\n449\t    - p vs. Previous\n450\t    rows:\n451\t    - - Frozen pi0\n452\t      - 0\n453\t      - 53.6\n454\t      - 1.8\n455\t      - '[51.4, 55.8]'\n456\t      - —\n457\t    - - Universal LoRA\n458\t      - ~2M\n459\t      - 65.4\n460\t      - 2.1\n461\t      - '[62.8, 68.0]'\n462\t      - <0.001\n463\t    - - Meta-Brain\n464\t      - ~6M\n465\t      - 71.4\n466\t      - 2.4\n467\t      - '[68.4, 74.4]'\n468\t      - '0.008'\n469\t    - - Oracle\n470\t      - ~6M\n471\t      - 75.3\n472\t      - 1.9\n473\t      - '[72.9, 77.7]'\n474\t      - '0.021'\n475\t  - name: Ablation Ladder — Per-Perturbation Breakdown (%, 5-seed mean)\n476\t    header:\n477\t    - Method\n478\t    - camera\n479\t    - light\n480\t    - bg\n481\t    - noise\n482\t    - distr\n483\t    - layout\n484\t    - robot\n485\t    - Overall\n486\t    rows:\n487\t    - - Frozen\n488\t      - 47.6\n489\t      - 56.2\n490\t      - 51.8\n491\t      - 49.4\n492\t      - 58.6\n493\t      - 57.8\n494\t      - 53.8\n495\t      - 53.6\n496\t    - - Universal\n497\t      - 62.8\n498\t      - 69.4\n499\t      - 66.2\n500\t      - 63.0\n501\t      - 64.8\n502\t      - 62.6\n503\t      - 69.0\n504\t      - 65.4\n505\t    - - Meta-Brain\n506\t      - 71.0\n507\t      - 77.6\n508\t      - 74.4\n509\t      - 73.0\n510\t      - 65.2\n511\t      - 64.4\n512\t      - 74.2\n513\t      - 71.4\n514\t    - - Oracle\n515\t      - 75.2\n516\t      - 82.0\n517\t      - 78.4\n518\t      - 77.6\n519\t      - 69.4\n520\t      - 66.6\n521\t      - 78.0\n522\t      - 75.3\n523\t  - name: Routing Gain Decomposition by Coarse Type\n524\t    header:\n525\t    - Coarse Type\n526\t    - Universal\n527\t    - Meta-Brain\n528\t    - Routing Gain\n529\t    - '% of Oracle Ceiling'\n530\t    rows:\n531\t    - - Visual (4 types)\n532\t      - 65.35\n533\t      - 74.0\n534\t      - 8.65\n535\t      - 66.8%\n536\t    - - Spatial (2 types)\n537\t      - 63.7\n538\t      - 64.8\n539\t      - 1.1\n540\t      - 25.6%\n541\t    - - Physical (1 type)\n542\t      - 69.0\n543\t      - 74.2\n544\t      - 5.2\n545\t      - 57.8%\n546\t    - - Overall\n547\t      - 65.4\n548\t      - 71.4\n549\t      - 6.0\n550\t      - 60.6%\n551\t  figures_description:\n552\t  - 'Stacked bar chart (the ablation ladder): 4 methods on x-axis, success rate on\n553\t    y-axis. Bars are colored in a gradient from red (Frozen) to green (Oracle). Error\n554\t    bars show ±1 std. Horizontal dashed lines at 81.2% (VLA-GSE reference) and 53.6%\n555\t    (Frozen baseline). Clear monotonic increase with decreasing step sizes. Significance\n556\t    brackets between adjacent pairs.\n557\t\n558\t    '\n559\t  - 'Per-perturbation grouped bar chart: 7 perturbation types on x-axis, 4 methods\n560\t    as grouped bars. Reveals the asymmetric routing benefit — large visual/physical\n561\t    separation between Universal and Meta-Brain bars, minimal spatial separation.\n562\t    Oracle bars highest across all types but layout/distractor gap is notably small.\n563\t\n564\t    '\n565\t  analysis: 'The ablation ladder is clean and publishable. All pairwise comparisons\n566\t    are significant. The key narrative point is that Meta-Brain captures 60.6% of\n567\t    the theoretically available routing benefit (oracle ceiling). The per-type decomposition\n568\t    reveals that routing works best where perturbations are localized (visual: 66.8%\n569\t    of ceiling captured) and least where perturbations are distributed (spatial: 25.6%).\n570\t    This naturally leads to the mechanistic analysis section in the paper explaining\n571\t    which processing stages each perturbation type disrupts. For Claim 2, the headline\n572\t    is: \"Routing by perturbation type improves over universal LoRA by 6.0 ± 2.3% (p\n573\t    = 0.008), with gains concentrated on perturbation types that disrupt localized\n574\t    processing stages.\" This reframing adds nuance rather than claiming universal\n575\t    superiority.\n576\t\n577\t    '\n578\t- name: FTM/FLA Reproduction — Visual-Only Baseline\n579\t  plan_id: plan_006\n580\t  description: 'Reproduce FTM (4K params) and FLA (4.7M params) on pi0 for visual\n581\t    perturbation types. Compare with LoRA-V and Meta-Brain to establish visual-only\n582\t    baselines and demonstrate Meta-Brain''s multi-type advantage.\n583\t\n584\t    '\n585\t  expected_results:\n586\t    ftm_camera: 69.8\n587\t    ftm_light: 76.4\n588\t    ftm_background: 72.6\n589\t    ftm_noise: 68.2\n590\t    ftm_visual_avg: 71.75\n591\t    ftm_overall: 65.3\n592\t    fla_camera: 73.8\n593\t    fla_light: 80.2\n594\t    fla_background: 76.8\n595\t    fla_noise: 75.4\n596\t    fla_visual_avg: 76.55\n597\t    fla_overall: 68.1\n598\t    lora_v_visual_avg: 78.3\n599\t    meta_brain_visual_avg: 74.0\n600\t    meta_brain_overall: 71.4\n601\t    meta_brain_advantage_over_ftm_overall: 6.1\n602\t    meta_brain_advantage_over_fla_overall: 3.3\n603\t  result_rationale: 'FTM at 4K params is remarkably parameter-efficient for visual\n604\t    perturbations (71.75% visual avg) but fundamentally cannot handle spatial/physical\n605\t    types, leaving those at frozen baseline levels and yielding only 65.3% overall.\n606\t    FLA at 4.7M params approaches LoRA-V quality on visual types (76.55% vs 78.3%)\n607\t    but also cannot generalize beyond visual. Meta-Brain''s overall advantage (71.4%\n608\t    vs 65.3-68.1%) comes entirely from spatial and physical perturbation handling.\n609\t    On visual types alone, LoRA-V (78.3%) > FLA (76.55%) > Meta-Brain routed (74.0%)\n610\t    > FTM (71.75%), showing that specialized visual methods can match or exceed routing-based\n611\t    correction for visual perturbations specifically. The key message: FTM/FLA are\n612\t    excellent visual-only solutions but cannot serve as general robustness methods.\n613\t    Meta-Brain''s value is breadth of coverage, not per-type optimality. FTM''s per-parameter\n614\t    efficiency on visual types (11.7%/0.004M = 2925%/M) dwarfs all other methods but\n615\t    is limited to a single perturbation modality.\n616\t\n617\t    '\n618\t  tables:\n619\t  - name: Visual Perturbation Methods Comparison (%)\n620\t    header:\n621\t    - Method\n622\t    - Params\n623\t    - camera\n624\t    - light\n625\t    - bg\n626\t    - noise\n627\t    - Visual Avg\n628\t    - Overall\n629\t    rows:\n630\t    - - FTM\n631\t      - 4K\n632\t      - 69.8\n633\t      - 76.4\n634\t      - 72.6\n635\t      - 68.2\n636\t      - 71.75\n637\t      - 65.3\n638\t    - - FLA\n639\t      - 4.7M\n640\t      - 73.8\n641\t      - 80.2\n642\t      - 76.8\n643\t      - 75.4\n644\t      - 76.55\n645\t      - 68.1\n646\t    - - LoRA-V\n647\t      - ~2M\n648\t      - 75.2\n649\t      - 82.0\n650\t      - 78.4\n651\t      - 77.6\n652\t      - 78.3\n653\t      - 67.4\n654\t    - - Meta-Brain\n655\t      - ~6M\n656\t      - 71.0\n657\t      - 77.6\n658\t      - 74.4\n659\t      - 73.0\n660\t      - 74.0\n661\t      - 71.4\n662\t    - - Universal\n663\t      - ~2M\n664\t      - 62.8\n665\t      - 69.4\n666\t      - 66.2\n667\t      - 63.0\n668\t      - 65.35\n669\t      - 65.4\n670\t  figures_description:\n671\t  - 'Two-panel figure. Left: visual-types-only comparison (4 visual perturbation bars\n672\t    per method). LoRA-V tops, FLA close second, Meta-Brain third, FTM fourth, Universal\n673\t    last. Right: overall LIBERO-Plus comparison. Meta-Brain tops (71.4%), FLA second\n674\t    (68.1%), LoRA-V/Universal/FTM clustered (65-67%). Shows the reversal: best visual-only\n675\t    method is not the best overall method.\n676\t\n677\t    '\n678\t  analysis: 'This experiment establishes two key points for the paper: (1) Visual-only\n679\t    methods are competitive on visual perturbations but fail as general robustness\n680\t    solutions — there is no free lunch. (2) Meta-Brain''s routing approach provides\n681\t    the best overall coverage by handling all perturbation types, even though it doesn''t\n682\t    maximize any single type. For Claim 3, FTM serves as an extreme point on the parameter-efficiency\n683\t    scatter plot: incredible visual-only efficiency but zero spatial/physical coverage.\n684\t    Meta-Brain occupies a qualitatively different position: moderate efficiency with\n685\t    universal coverage.\n686\t\n687\t    '\n688\t- name: Parameter Efficiency Analysis\n689\t  plan_id: plan_007\n690\t  description: 'Compute gain-over-frozen per method, normalize by trainable parameters.\n691\t    Produce the parameter efficiency scatter plot (x=params log scale, y=gain-over-baseline).\n692\t    Include Meta-Brain, Universal LoRA, FTM, FLA, VLA-GSE (from paper, different backbone\n693\t    caveat).\n694\t\n695\t    '\n696\t  expected_results:\n697\t    meta_brain_gain: 17.8\n698\t    meta_brain_params_M: 6\n699\t    meta_brain_gain_per_M: 2.97\n700\t    universal_gain: 11.8\n701\t    universal_params_M: 2\n702\t    universal_gain_per_M: 5.9\n703\t    ftm_gain: 11.7\n704\t    ftm_params_M: 0.004\n705\t    ftm_gain_per_M: 2925.0\n706\t    fla_gain: 14.5\n707\t    fla_params_M: 4.7\n708\t    fla_gain_per_M: 3.09\n709\t    vla_gse_gain: 27.6\n710\t    vla_gse_params_M: 114\n711\t    vla_gse_gain_per_M: 0.24\n712\t    meta_brain_pct_of_vla_gse_gain: 64.5\n713\t    meta_brain_pct_of_vla_gse_params: 5.3\n714\t  result_rationale: 'Meta-Brain achieves 2.97%/M gain-per-parameter, sitting in the\n715\t    middle of the efficiency spectrum. Universal LoRA is the most efficient multi-type\n716\t    method (5.9%/M) but has a lower absolute gain ceiling. FTM is an extreme outlier\n717\t    (2925%/M) demonstrating that ultra-compact methods exist for single-type perturbations,\n718\t    but this efficiency doesn''t scale to multi-type coverage. VLA-GSE achieves the\n719\t    highest absolute gain (27.6%) but at 0.24%/M efficiency — a 12× parameter overhead\n720\t    vs Meta-Brain for 55% more gain. The headline for Claim 3: \"Meta-Brain achieves\n721\t    64.5% of VLA-GSE''s robustness improvement using 5.3% of its trainable parameters,\n722\t    demonstrating perturbation-diagnostic routing as a parameter-efficient alternative\n723\t    to capacity-based expert routing.\" The different-backbone caveat (pi0 vs Qwen3-VL-4B)\n724\t    applies to absolute numbers but the efficiency ratio is still informative.\n725\t\n726\t    '\n727\t  tables:\n728\t  - name: Parameter Efficiency Comparison\n729\t    header:\n730\t    - Method\n731\t    - Backbone\n732\t    - Params (M)\n733\t    - Gain over Frozen (%)\n734\t    - Gain/M Params\n735\t    - Coverage\n736\t    rows:\n737\t    - - FTM\n738\t      - pi0\n739\t      - 0.004\n740\t      - 11.7\n741\t      - 2925.0\n742\t      - Visual only\n743\t    - - Universal LoRA\n744\t      - pi0\n745\t      - 2\n746\t      - 11.8\n747\t      - 5.9\n748\t      - All types\n749\t    - - FLA\n750\t      - pi0\n751\t      - 4.7\n752\t      - 14.5\n753\t      - 3.09\n754\t      - Visual only\n755\t    - - Meta-Brain\n756\t      - pi0\n757\t      - 6\n758\t      - 17.8\n759\t      - 2.97\n760\t      - All types\n761\t    - - VLA-GSE†\n762\t      - Qwen3-VL-4B\n763\t      - 114\n764\t      - 27.6\n765\t      - 0.24\n766\t      - All types\n767\t  figures_description:\n768\t  - 'Scatter plot: x-axis = trainable parameters (log scale, 0.001M to 200M), y-axis\n769\t    = gain over frozen baseline (%). Each method is a labeled point with marker size\n770\t    proportional to coverage (all-type methods larger). FTM is far left (tiny params,\n771\t    moderate gain). Universal LoRA and Meta-Brain are center-left. VLA-GSE is far\n772\t    right (high gain, huge params). A Pareto frontier line connects FTM → Universal\n773\t    → Meta-Brain, showing that Meta-Brain extends the efficiency frontier beyond universal\n774\t    adaptation. VLA-GSE sits above the frontier but at 19× the cost. Dashed diagonal\n775\t    lines show iso-efficiency contours (%/M). Annotation: \"Meta-Brain: 65% of VLA-GSE\n776\t    gain at 5% parameters.\" VLA-GSE point marked with † for different backbone.\n777\t\n778\t    '\n779\t  analysis: 'The scatter plot is the visual centerpiece of Claim 3. The key insight\n780\t    is that Meta-Brain extends the Pareto frontier established by Universal LoRA —\n781\t    it proves that routing-based specialization extracts more gain per parameter than\n782\t    simply increasing uniform LoRA rank. The framing should be \"complementary to capacity\n783\t    routing, not replacement\": Meta-Brain operates in a different region of the parameter-efficiency\n784\t    space than VLA-GSE. For resource-constrained deployment (edge devices, real-time\n785\t    control), Meta-Brain offers a practical operating point. An ideal system might\n786\t    compose both: Meta-Brain for type-aware correction + capacity routing for residual\n787\t    error.\n788\t\n789\t    '\n790\t- name: Correction Memory Ablation — With/Without CM\n791\t  plan_id: plan_008\n792\t  description: 'Compare Meta-Brain with and without Correction Memory module. CM modulates\n793\t    routing weights using retrieved exemplars from a FAISS-indexed memory bank. Quantify\n794\t    marginal gain overall and per perturbation type.\n795\t\n796\t    '\n797\t  expected_results:\n798\t    meta_brain_no_cm: 71.4\n799\t    meta_brain_with_cm: 72.6\n800\t    cm_ablation_delta: 1.2\n801\t    cm_delta_visual: 0.8\n802\t    cm_delta_spatial: 0.4\n803\t    cm_delta_physical: 2.8\n804\t    cm_alpha_learned: 0.23\n805\t    cm_retrieval_latency_ms: 1.4\n806\t  result_rationale: 'CM provides a marginal +1.2% overall gain, concentrated on physical\n807\t    perturbations (+2.8%) where the same robot dynamics changes recur consistently\n808\t    across episodes — exemplar retrieval identifies \"I''ve seen this perturbation\n809\t    before\" and sharpens the routing weight toward LoRA-P. Visual gain is small (+0.8%)\n810\t    because the PAR router already routes visual perturbations confidently (diag 0.82)\n811\t    and CM''s modulation has little room to improve. Spatial gain is minimal (+0.4%)\n812\t    because spatial perturbations are fundamentally different each time (different\n813\t    object positions) so retrieved exemplars provide weak signal. The learned alpha\n814\t    parameter (0.23) confirms the system''s own assessment: CM contributes ~23% weighting\n815\t    to the final routing decision, indicating it''s a secondary correction to PAR,\n816\t    not a primary signal. The 1.4ms retrieval latency adds negligible overhead to\n817\t    the 10Hz control loop. CM is worth including as an optional module but does not\n818\t    change the core story.\n819\t\n820\t    '\n821\t  tables:\n822\t  - name: Correction Memory Ablation (%)\n823\t    header:\n824\t    - Configuration\n825\t    - Visual\n826\t    - Spatial\n827\t    - Physical\n828\t    - Overall\n829\t    rows:\n830\t    - - Meta-Brain (no CM)\n831\t      - 74.0\n832\t      - 64.8\n833\t      - 74.2\n834\t      - 71.4\n835\t    - - Meta-Brain + CM\n836\t      - 74.8\n837\t      - 65.2\n838\t      - 77.0\n839\t      - 72.6\n840\t    - - CM Delta\n841\t      - 0.8\n842\t      - 0.4\n843\t      - 2.8\n844\t      - 1.2\n845\t  figures_description:\n846\t  - 'Grouped bar chart: 3 coarse types + overall on x-axis, paired bars (with/without\n847\t    CM). Physical bar shows visible CM benefit. Visual and spatial bars nearly identical.\n848\t    Error bars from 3 seeds. The difference is within 1 std for visual/spatial but\n849\t    marginally significant for physical.\n850\t\n851\t    '\n852\t  analysis: 'CM''s marginal contribution (1.2%) is expected in the median tier. It\n853\t    validates the module as a sound idea (positive delta on all types) but not a paper-defining\n854\t    contribution. Present CM as \"optional module, +1.2% overall, primarily benefiting\n855\t    recurrent physical perturbations.\" The per-type pattern adds a small mechanistic\n856\t    insight: exemplar-based routing modulation works best when perturbations are consistent\n857\t    (physics changes) rather than combinatorially varied (spatial layouts). For the\n858\t    paper, CM goes in the ablation section with 1-2 sentences, not a dedicated section.\n859\t\n860\t    '\n861\t- name: Router Architecture Comparison — MLP vs Linear vs Attention\n862\t  plan_id: plan_009\n863\t  description: 'Compare PAR router variants on PaliGemma layer 6: (a) 2-layer MLP\n864\t    (default, ~50K params), (b) linear classifier (~6K params), (c) cross-attention\n865\t    router (~120K params). Evaluate both routing accuracy and downstream task success\n866\t    to test whether classification accuracy improvements translate to task performance.\n867\t\n868\t    '\n869\t  expected_results:\n870\t    mlp_routing_accuracy: 93.8\n871\t    mlp_task_success: 71.4\n872\t    mlp_params: 50000\n873\t    linear_routing_accuracy: 90.6\n874\t    linear_task_success: 70.2\n875\t    linear_params: 6000\n876\t    attention_routing_accuracy: 94.2\n877\t    attention_task_success: 71.2\n878\t    attention_params: 120000\n879\t    mlp_vs_linear_task_gap: 1.2\n880\t    mlp_vs_attention_task_gap: 0.2\n881\t  result_rationale: 'MLP (default) achieves 93.8% routing accuracy and 71.4% task\n882\t    success, offering the best cost/performance tradeoff. Linear router loses 3.2%\n883\t    routing accuracy, which translates to a modest 1.2% task success drop — the per-token\n884\t    representation at layer 6 is already quite separable (Phase 0 showed F1=0.993\n885\t    with MLP), so a linear boundary captures most of the structure but misses some\n886\t    nonlinear decision boundaries near cluster edges. Attention router adds 0.4% routing\n887\t    accuracy over MLP (the classes are well-separated enough that attention over token\n888\t    sequences adds minimal information beyond mean pooling) but this doesn''t translate\n889\t    to task success improvement (71.2% vs 71.4%) — the 0.4% classification gain falls\n890\t    within the noise floor of rollout evaluation. The attention router''s 2.4× parameter\n891\t    overhead is unjustified. Conclusion: MLP is the right choice, confirming the Phase\n892\t    0 finding that perturbation type is a simple classification problem at layer 6.\n893\t\n894\t    '\n895\t  tables:\n896\t  - name: Router Architecture Comparison\n897\t    header:\n898\t    - Router\n899\t    - Params\n900\t    - Routing Acc (%)\n901\t    - Task Success (%)\n902\t    - Inference Overhead (ms)\n903\t    rows:\n904\t    - - Linear\n905\t      - 6K\n906\t      - 90.6\n907\t      - 70.2\n908\t      - 0.02\n909\t    - - MLP (default)\n910\t      - 50K\n911\t      - 93.8\n912\t      - 71.4\n913\t      - 0.05\n914\t    - - Cross-Attention\n915\t      - 120K\n916\t      - 94.2\n917\t      - 71.2\n918\t      - 0.18\n919\t  figures_description:\n920\t  - 'Dual-axis scatter: x = routing classification accuracy (%), left y = task success\n921\t    (%), right y = router parameter count. Three points (Linear, MLP, Attention).\n922\t    Shows that routing accuracy improvements beyond ~93% yield diminishing task success\n923\t    returns. The gap between routing accuracy and task success is largest for Attention,\n924\t    illustrating the disconnect between classification metrics and control metrics.\n925\t\n926\t    '\n927\t  analysis: 'This experiment addresses reviewer concern C1 (\"Phase 0 classification\n928\t    is too easy\") from a different angle: yes, the classification is relatively easy\n929\t    (even a linear classifier gets 90.6%), but the task-success gap between 90.6%\n930\t    and 93.8% routing accuracy is 1.2% — confirming that routing accuracy does matter\n931\t    at the margins. The MLP''s 3.2% classification advantage over linear translates\n932\t    to 1.2% task success gain, roughly 1:0.37 ratio. Beyond 93.8%, additional classification\n933\t    gains have near-zero marginal task benefit. This helps calibrate the oracle-PAR\n934\t    gap analysis: the 3.9% task gap from oracle routing quality corresponds to moving\n935\t    from ~93.8% to ~100% classification accuracy, and the nonlinear mapping suggests\n936\t    diminishing returns as routing approaches perfection.\n937\t\n938\t    '\n939\t- name: 6-Class vs 3-Class Routing Comparison\n940\t  plan_id: plan_010\n941\t  description: 'Compare fine-grained 6-class routing (camera/light/background/noise/layout/robot,\n942\t    6 LoRA experts ~12M params) with coarse 3-class routing (Visual/Spatial/Physical,\n943\t    3 experts ~6M). Tests whether finer-grained perturbation-type routing justifies\n944\t    additional parameters and architectural complexity.\n945\t\n946\t    '\n947\t  expected_results:\n948\t    three_class_overall: 71.4\n949\t    three_class_routing_accuracy: 93.8\n950\t    three_class_params_M: 6\n951\t    six_class_overall: 72.2\n952\t    six_class_routing_accuracy: 89.4\n953\t    six_class_params_M: 12\n954\t    delta_overall: 0.8\n955\t    six_class_camera: 72.8\n956\t    six_class_light: 79.2\n957\t    six_class_background: 76.0\n958\t    six_class_noise: 74.6\n959\t    six_class_distractor: 66.0\n960\t    six_class_layout: 65.2\n961\t    six_class_robot: 81.6\n962\t  result_rationale: '6-class routing provides only +0.8% overall improvement over\n963\t    3-class while doubling the parameter budget (12M vs 6M) and dropping routing accuracy\n964\t    by 4.4% (89.4% vs 93.8%). The marginal gain arises primarily from the robot expert\n965\t    (+3.8% from dedicated robot LoRA vs shared Physical LoRA) where the 1-type Physical\n966\t    class benefits from fully dedicated parameters. Intra-Visual perturbation types\n967\t    (camera/light/background/noise) do NOT benefit significantly from separate experts\n968\t    because they share the same failure mode (early representation corruption) — Phase\n969\t    0 6-class analysis already showed high intra-Visual similarity. The spatial split\n970\t    (distractor/layout) gains marginally because both types require trajectory-level\n971\t    reasoning that LoRA cannot provide. The 4.4% routing accuracy drop with 6 classes\n972\t    partially offsets any per-expert specialization gain: more classes means more\n973\t    routing errors, and each error routes to a more narrowly specialized (thus more\n974\t    harmful when mismatched) expert. Net assessment: 3-class is the better design\n975\t    point.\n976\t\n977\t    '\n978\t  tables:\n979\t  - name: 6-Class vs 3-Class Comparison (%)\n980\t    header:\n981\t    - Configuration\n982\t    - Classes\n983\t    - Params\n984\t    - Routing Acc\n985\t    - Overall\n986\t    - Δ vs 3-class\n987\t    rows:\n988\t    - - 3-class Meta-Brain\n989\t      - 3\n990\t      - ~6M\n991\t      - 93.8\n992\t      - 71.4\n993\t      - —\n994\t    - - 6-class Meta-Brain\n995\t      - 6\n996\t      - ~12M\n997\t      - 89.4\n998\t      - 72.2\n999\t      - 0.8\n1000\t  - name: 6-Class Per-Type Breakdown vs 3-Class (%)\n1001\t    header:\n1002\t    - Perturbation\n1003\t    - 3-class\n1004\t    - 6-class\n1005\t    - Delta\n1006\t    rows:\n1007\t    - - camera\n1008\t      - 71.0\n1009\t      - 72.8\n1010\t      - 1.8\n1011\t    - - light\n1012\t      - 77.6\n1013\t      - 79.2\n1014\t      - 1.6\n1015\t    - - background\n1016\t      - 74.4\n1017\t      - 76.0\n1018\t      - 1.6\n1019\t    - - noise\n1020\t      - 73.0\n1021\t      - 74.6\n1022\t      - 1.6\n1023\t    - - distractor\n1024\t      - 65.2\n1025\t      - 66.0\n1026\t      - 0.8\n1027\t    - - layout\n1028\t      - 64.4\n1029\t      - 65.2\n1030\t      - 0.8\n1031\t    - - robot\n1032\t      - 74.2\n1033\t      - 81.6\n1034\t      - 7.4\n1035\t  figures_description:\n1036\t  - 'Stacked cost-benefit bar: left bar = 3-class (6M params, 71.4% success), right\n1037\t    bar = 6-class (12M params, 72.2% success). The 2× parameter cost is visually dominant\n1038\t    for a barely visible success rate gain. Annotation: \"+0.8% for 2× params = poor\n1039\t    ROI.\"\n1040\t\n1041\t    '\n1042\t  analysis: 'This directly addresses reviewer concern C5 (\"3-class taxonomy may be\n1043\t    too coarse\"). The answer is: 3-class is nearly optimal for this architecture.\n1044\t    The 6-class robot improvement (+7.4%) is notable in isolation but doesn''t offset\n1045\t    the systemic costs of finer routing. The Phase 0 intra-Visual similarity finding\n1046\t    (6-class accuracy 99.82% but intra-Visual confusion is near-zero) predicted this\n1047\t    outcome: types that cluster together in activation space don''t need separate\n1048\t    experts. Include this as a 1-paragraph ablation result: \"Finer 6-class routing\n1049\t    adds +0.8% at 2× parameters, confirming that the 3-class taxonomy aligns with\n1050\t    the mechanistic distinction in VLA processing stages.\"\n1051\t\n1052\t    '\n1053\t- name: Cross-Backbone Validation — SmolVLA\n1054\t  plan_id: plan_011\n1055\t  description: 'Replicate Phase 0 classification + Phase 1 routing pipeline on SmolVLA\n1056\t    to test whether perturbation-diagnostic routing generalizes beyond pi0. SmolVLA\n1057\t    uses a different vision encoder (SigLIP) and language backbone (SmolLM), testing\n1058\t    architecture independence.\n1059\t\n1060\t    '\n1061\t  expected_results:\n1062\t    smolvla_phase0_3class_f1: 0.938\n1063\t    smolvla_phase0_best_layer: 4\n1064\t    smolvla_frozen_baseline: 46.2\n1065\t    smolvla_universal_lora: 56.8\n1066\t    smolvla_meta_brain: 62.4\n1067\t    smolvla_gain_over_frozen: 16.2\n1068\t    smolvla_gain_over_universal: 5.6\n1069\t    smolvla_routing_diagonality: 0.73\n1070\t    smolvla_visual_specialization_delta: 10.4\n1071\t    smolvla_spatial_specialization_delta: 2.8\n1072\t    smolvla_physical_specialization_delta: 7.6\n1073\t  result_rationale: 'SmolVLA confirms the core finding: frozen VLA activations encode\n1074\t    perturbation type (F1=0.938, lower than pi0''s 0.993 due to SigLIP''s different\n1075\t    feature structure but still high). The best classification layer shifts to layer\n1076\t    4 (SmolVLA has fewer layers than PaliGemma). Meta-Brain on SmolVLA achieves +16.2%\n1077\t    gain over frozen (comparable to pi0''s +17.8%) and +5.6% over universal (comparable\n1078\t    to pi0''s +6.0%), demonstrating that the routing benefit is architecture-independent.\n1079\t    Absolute numbers are lower (62.4% vs 71.4%) due to SmolVLA''s weaker backbone\n1080\t    capacity (SmolLM-360M vs pi0''s larger model). The per-type specialization pattern\n1081\t    replicates: visual shows the largest delta (10.4%), physical moderate (7.6%),\n1082\t    spatial weak (2.8%). Spatial underperformance persists across backbones, confirming\n1083\t    it''s a fundamental limitation of single-step LoRA correction for trajectory-level\n1084\t    perturbations, not an artifact of pi0''s architecture. Routing diagonality (0.73)\n1085\t    is slightly lower than pi0 (0.77), reflecting SigLIP''s less structured intermediate\n1086\t    representations for perturbation classification.\n1087\t\n1088\t    '\n1089\t  tables:\n1090\t  - name: Cross-Backbone Comparison (pi0 vs SmolVLA)\n1091\t    header:\n1092\t    - Metric\n1093\t    - pi0\n1094\t    - SmolVLA\n1095\t    rows:\n1096\t    - - Phase 0 3-class F1\n1097\t      - 0.993\n1098\t      - 0.938\n1099\t    - - Best classification layer\n1100\t      - 6\n1101\t      - 4\n1102\t    - - Frozen baseline (%)\n1103\t      - 53.6\n1104\t      - 46.2\n1105\t    - - Universal LoRA (%)\n1106\t      - 65.4\n1107\t      - 56.8\n1108\t    - - Meta-Brain (%)\n1109\t      - 71.4\n1110\t      - 62.4\n1111\t    - - Gain over frozen (%)\n1112\t      - 17.8\n1113\t      - 16.2\n1114\t    - - Gain over universal (%)\n1115\t      - 6.0\n1116\t      - 5.6\n1117\t    - - Routing diagonality\n1118\t      - 0.77\n1119\t      - 0.73\n1120\t    - - Visual specialization delta (%)\n1121\t      - 12.95\n1122\t      - 10.4\n1123\t    - - Spatial specialization delta (%)\n1124\t      - 4.3\n1125\t      - 2.8\n1126\t  figures_description:\n1127\t  - 'Side-by-side ablation ladders for pi0 and SmolVLA. Both show the same monotonic\n1128\t    ordering (Frozen < Universal < Meta-Brain) with similar step sizes. Pi0 bars are\n1129\t    uniformly higher (stronger backbone) but the relative gains are comparable. Annotation\n1130\t    highlights the consistent routing benefit across architectures.\n1131\t\n1132\t    '\n1133\t  analysis: 'This experiment addresses reviewer concern C3 (\"single backbone, limited\n1134\t    generalizability\"). The result is clearly positive: the qualitative pattern replicates\n1135\t    exactly (same per-type specialization ranking, same ablation ordering, comparable\n1136\t    relative gains). The Phase 0 F1 drop (0.993 → 0.938) is expected — SigLIP and\n1137\t    PaliGemma have different feature structures — but 0.938 is still high enough for\n1138\t    effective routing. The spatial underperformance replication across backbones strengthens\n1139\t    the mechanistic interpretation: it''s a property of the perturbation type, not\n1140\t    the backbone. For the paper, include as a validation subsection: \"Cross-backbone\n1141\t    results on SmolVLA replicate the qualitative findings, with comparable routing\n1142\t    gains (+5.6% vs +6.0% over universal), confirming that perturbation-diagnostic\n1143\t    routing is an architecture-independent principle.\" This is a P2 experiment — include\n1144\t    if time/GPU budget permits, otherwise cite the Phase 0 cross-backbone evidence\n1145\t    from SAFE/probing literature.\n1146\t\n1147\t    '\n1148\t- name: LoRA Layer Placement Ablation\n1149\t  plan_id: plan_012\n1150\t  description: 'Vary which PaliGemma layers receive LoRA: (a) early (2-6), (b) mid\n1151\t    (6-12), (c) late (12-16), (d) all layers. Test hypothesis that perturbation types\n1152\t    optimally correct at different processing stages.\n1153\t\n1154\t    '\n1155\t  expected_results:\n1156\t    lora_v_early: 80.2\n1157\t    lora_v_mid: 74.8\n1158\t    lora_v_late: 71.4\n1159\t    lora_v_all: 78.3\n1160\t    lora_s_early: 64.6\n1161\t    lora_s_mid: 70.2\n1162\t    lora_s_late: 66.8\n1163\t    lora_s_all: 68.0\n1164\t    lora_p_early: 72.8\n1165\t    lora_p_mid: 75.2\n1166\t    lora_p_late: 80.6\n1167\t    lora_p_all: 78.0\n1168\t    optimal_placement_v: early (2-6)\n1169\t    optimal_placement_s: mid (6-12)\n1170\t    optimal_placement_p: late (12-16)\n1171\t    optimal_combined_overall: 73.8\n1172\t    all_layer_combined_overall: 71.4\n1173\t    layer_placement_gain: 2.4\n1174\t  result_rationale: 'The layer placement results support the mechanistic hypothesis\n1175\t    with moderate effect sizes. LoRA-V benefits most from early layers (+1.9% over\n1176\t    all-layer) because visual perturbations (camera/light/background/noise) corrupt\n1177\t    the initial visual encoding in PaliGemma''s early layers — correcting at the source\n1178\t    prevents error propagation. LoRA-S benefits from mid layers (+2.2% over all-layer)\n1179\t    because spatial reasoning (object relationships, layout understanding) is computed\n1180\t    in middle transformer layers where multi-head attention integrates spatial context\n1181\t    — though the absolute improvement remains modest due to the fundamental trajectory-level\n1182\t    limitation. LoRA-P benefits from late layers (+2.6% over all-layer) because physical\n1183\t    perturbations manifest at the action prediction stage in late layers where dynamics\n1184\t    models are implicitly computed. All-layer placement performs as a reasonable default\n1185\t    (second-best for each expert type) because the LoRA rank is distributed across\n1186\t    layers that contribute varying amounts. The combined optimal placement (type-specific\n1187\t    layers per expert) yields 73.8% overall (+2.4% over uniform all-layer 71.4%),\n1188\t    suggesting layer-aware routing is a promising extension.\n1189\t\n1190\t    '\n1191\t  tables:\n1192\t  - name: Layer Placement × Expert Type (own-type success rate %)\n1193\t    header:\n1194\t    - Layer Range\n1195\t    - LoRA-V (Visual)\n1196\t    - LoRA-S (Spatial)\n1197\t    - LoRA-P (Physical)\n1198\t    rows:\n1199\t    - - Early (2-6)\n1200\t      - 80.2\n1201\t      - 64.6\n1202\t      - 72.8\n1203\t    - - Mid (6-12)\n1204\t      - 74.8\n1205\t      - 70.2\n1206\t      - 75.2\n1207\t    - - Late (12-16)\n1208\t      - 71.4\n1209\t      - 66.8\n1210\t      - 80.6\n1211\t    - - All layers\n1212\t      - 78.3\n1213\t      - 68.0\n1214\t      - 78.0\n1215\t  - name: Optimal Layer Placement Summary\n1216\t    header:\n1217\t    - Expert\n1218\t    - Best Layers\n1219\t    - Own-Type Success\n1220\t    - Δ vs All-Layer\n1221\t    rows:\n1222\t    - - LoRA-V\n1223\t      - Early (2-6)\n1224\t      - 80.2\n1225\t      - 1.9\n1226\t    - - LoRA-S\n1227\t      - Mid (6-12)\n1228\t      - 70.2\n1229\t      - 2.2\n1230\t    - - LoRA-P\n1231\t      - Late (12-16)\n1232\t      - 80.6\n1233\t      - 2.6\n1234\t  figures_description:\n1235\t  - '3-panel line chart: one panel per expert type. X-axis = layer range (early/mid/late/all),\n1236\t    y-axis = own-type success rate. Each panel shows a different peak: LoRA-V peaks\n1237\t    early, LoRA-S peaks mid, LoRA-P peaks late. All-layer performance marked with\n1238\t    a dashed horizontal line in each panel for reference. The crossed peak pattern\n1239\t    visually demonstrates that different perturbation types optimally correct at different\n1240\t    processing stages.\n1241\t\n1242\t    '\n1243\t  analysis: 'This is a P2 experiment that adds mechanistic depth but is not essential\n1244\t    for the core claims. The crossed peak pattern (V-early, S-mid, P-late) aligns\n1245\t    with how VLA processing stages work: visual encoding → spatial reasoning → action\n1246\t    prediction. This provides evidence for the paper''s framing that perturbation\n1247\t    types disrupt different processing stages. The +2.4% gain from optimal layer placement\n1248\t    is small but suggests a natural extension: layer-aware routing that not only selects\n1249\t    the right expert but applies it at the right layers. This could close part of\n1250\t    the oracle-PAR gap (3.9%) without improving classification accuracy. For the paper,\n1251\t    include as a supplementary analysis with the crossed-peak figure — it''s visually\n1252\t    compelling and mechanistically interpretive. Do not pursue layer-specific routing\n1253\t    as a primary contribution; it''s a natural future work direction.'\n1254\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01LQ4Te7gZVbHZuRYt6tuXWZ","session_id":"f3c89458-961d-4d5e-a388-373831b4983c","uuid":"dd81e58f-ebf7-4b30-94d5-4f20916550ea","timestamp":"2026-05-15T16:39:20.901Z"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01BmL3SM7TbNkGUJep9UcQpb","type":"tool_result","content":"1\tnarrative_guidance: 'Original framing holds as-is. Headline: Meta-Brain achieves 78.4%\n2\t  on LIBERO-Plus  with 6M params (80.8% with CM), closing 90% of the gap to VLA-GSE\n3\t  (81.2%, 114M params)  at 19x fewer trainable parameters. All three claims land cleanly\n4\t  — Phase 0 diagnosability  enables zero-overhead routing (Claim 1), the ablation\n5\t  ladder shows targeted > uniform  correction with 13.6% gain over universal LoRA\n6\t  (Claim 2), and the parameter efficiency  scatter plot positions Meta-Brain at 4.13\n7\t  gain/M-param vs VLA-GSE''s 0.24 (Claim 3).  Specialization is validated by 20% max\n8\t  delta (camera type) and strong cross-type  degradation of mismatched experts. Oracle-PAR\n9\t  gap of 1.2% confirms Phase 0 signal is  actionable. Paper should lead with the ablation\n10\t  ladder figure and close with the  parameter-efficiency scatter plot.\n11\t\n12\t  '\n13\timagined_experiments:\n14\t- name: LoRA expert training — 3 specialized + 1 universal\n15\t  plan_id: plan_002\n16\t  description: 'Train 4 LoRA adapters (rank 16) on frozen pi0 PaliGemma layers: LoRA-V\n17\t    (Visual),  LoRA-S (Spatial), LoRA-P (Physical), Universal LoRA (mixed). Evaluate\n18\t    each on  own-type and cross-type perturbations.\n19\t\n20\t    '\n21\t  expected_results:\n22\t    lora_v_visual_avg: 76.0\n23\t    lora_v_camera: 74.0\n24\t    lora_v_light: 80.0\n25\t    lora_v_background: 78.0\n26\t    lora_v_noise: 72.0\n27\t    lora_v_on_spatial: 60.0\n28\t    lora_v_on_physical: 54.0\n29\t    lora_s_layout: 90.0\n30\t    lora_s_on_visual_avg: 46.5\n31\t    lora_s_on_physical: 56.0\n32\t    lora_p_robot: 88.0\n33\t    lora_p_on_visual_avg: 44.0\n34\t    lora_p_on_spatial: 62.0\n35\t    universal_lora_overall: 64.8\n36\t    universal_camera: 54.0\n37\t    universal_light: 66.0\n38\t    universal_background: 62.0\n39\t    universal_noise: 54.0\n40\t    universal_layout: 78.0\n41\t    universal_robot: 74.0\n42\t    per_type_specialization_delta_max: 20.0\n43\t    per_type_specialization_delta_min: 12.0\n44\t    cross_type_degradation_max: -20.0\n45\t  result_rationale: 'Rank-16 LoRA on PaliGemma layers provides足够的修正容量处理单一扰动类型。 专用\n46\t    LoRA 在其目标类型上大幅超越 universal LoRA（最大 delta=20%，camera 类型），因为： (1) Visual 扰动主要破坏\n47\t    PaliGemma 早期视觉编码，LoRA-V 的全部容量用于修复这一信号通路， 而 universal LoRA 必须将同样容量分摊到三类截然不同的校正模式上；\n48\t    (2) Spatial (layout) 扰动修改物体空间关系，LoRA-S 学到的校正向量直接对齐中层空间表征， 在 layout 上达 90%——这是所有组合中最高的，因为\n49\t    layout 是单一子类、分布集中； (3) Physical (robot) 扰动改变力学属性，LoRA-P 在 robot 上达 88%。 Cross-type\n50\t    严重退化（LoRA-V 在 physical 仅 54%，低于 frozen baseline 的 56%）证实 三类扰动所需的校正模式确实互不兼容——这是\n51\t    Claim 2 的关键论据：专用路由并非锦上添花， 而是必要条件。Universal LoRA 在 64.8% 饱和，因为 rank-16 的有限容量在三类矛盾梯度\n52\t    方向间折衷，导致每种类型都欠校正。\n53\t\n54\t    '\n55\t  tables:\n56\t  - name: Expert cross-evaluation matrix\n57\t    columns:\n58\t    - Expert\n59\t    - camera\n60\t    - light\n61\t    - background\n62\t    - noise\n63\t    - layout\n64\t    - robot\n65\t    - Overall\n66\t    rows:\n67\t    - - LoRA-V\n68\t      - 74.0\n69\t      - 80.0\n70\t      - 78.0\n71\t      - 72.0\n72\t      - 60.0\n73\t      - 54.0\n74\t      - 69.7\n75\t    - - LoRA-S\n76\t      - 44.0\n77\t      - 52.0\n78\t      - 48.0\n79\t      - 42.0\n80\t      - 90.0\n81\t      - 56.0\n82\t      - 55.3\n83\t    - - LoRA-P\n84\t      - 40.0\n85\t      - 50.0\n86\t      - 46.0\n87\t      - 40.0\n88\t      - 62.0\n89\t      - 88.0\n90\t      - 54.3\n91\t    - - Universal\n92\t      - 54.0\n93\t      - 66.0\n94\t      - 62.0\n95\t      - 54.0\n96\t      - 78.0\n97\t      - 74.0\n98\t      - 64.8\n99\t    - - Frozen pi0\n100\t      - 42.0\n101\t      - 58.0\n102\t      - 52.0\n103\t      - 46.0\n104\t      - 68.0\n105\t      - 56.0\n106\t      - 53.6\n107\t  - name: Specialization delta (own-type expert minus universal)\n108\t    columns:\n109\t    - Perturbation type\n110\t    - Specialist\n111\t    - Universal\n112\t    - Delta\n113\t    rows:\n114\t    - - camera\n115\t      - 74.0\n116\t      - 54.0\n117\t      - '+20.0'\n118\t    - - light\n119\t      - 80.0\n120\t      - 66.0\n121\t      - '+14.0'\n122\t    - - background\n123\t      - 78.0\n124\t      - 62.0\n125\t      - '+16.0'\n126\t    - - noise\n127\t      - 72.0\n128\t      - 54.0\n129\t      - '+18.0'\n130\t    - - layout\n131\t      - 90.0\n132\t      - 78.0\n133\t      - '+12.0'\n134\t    - - robot\n135\t      - 88.0\n136\t      - 74.0\n137\t      - '+14.0'\n138\t  figures_description:\n139\t  - 'Heatmap: 3×6 cross-evaluation matrix (expert rows × perturbation columns), strong\n140\t    diagonal blocks visible — LoRA-V hot on left 4 columns, LoRA-S hot on layout,\n141\t    LoRA-P hot on robot. Off-diagonal cells cool/cold, many below frozen baseline.'\n142\t  - 'Grouped bar chart: per-type success rate for each expert + universal + frozen,\n143\t    clearly showing each specialist dominates its own types while failing on others.'\n144\t  analysis: '最核心发现：cross-type 退化的幅度（最大 -20% vs frozen）与 own-type 提升幅度（最大 +20%） 几乎对称，说明\n145\t    LoRA 学到的不是通用「鲁棒性」而是类型特异的校正映射。 Universal LoRA 在每个类型上都不如对应专家，差距最大的是 camera（-20）和\n146\t    noise（-18）， 最小的是 layout（-12）。Layout 差距最小因为它是 Spatial 类的唯一子类型，universal LoRA  分配给\n147\t    spatial 校正的有效容量比例相对较高。这为 Meta-Brain 的路由设计提供了直接动机： 如果能正确识别扰动类型并激活对应专家，就能同时获得所有类型上的最优校正。\n148\t\n149\t    '\n150\t- name: Meta-Brain assembly — PAR + LoRA bank E2E\n151\t  plan_id: plan_003\n152\t  description: 'Assemble PAR router (PaliGemma layer 6 MLP) + 3 frozen LoRA experts\n153\t    with soft routing.  Fine-tune only PAR routing weights end-to-end on LIBERO-Plus\n154\t    rollouts.\n155\t\n156\t    '\n157\t  expected_results:\n158\t    libero_plus_overall: 78.4\n159\t    camera: 72.0\n160\t    light: 78.0\n161\t    background: 76.0\n162\t    noise: 70.0\n163\t    layout: 88.0\n164\t    robot: 86.0\n165\t    visual_avg: 74.0\n166\t    spatial_avg: 88.0\n167\t    physical_avg: 86.0\n168\t    routing_diagonality: 0.92\n169\t    par_visual_weight_on_lora_v: 0.91\n170\t    par_spatial_weight_on_lora_s: 0.93\n171\t    par_physical_weight_on_lora_p: 0.92\n172\t    trainable_params_M: 6.1\n173\t    routing_params_K: 48\n174\t    gain_over_frozen: 24.8\n175\t    gain_over_universal_lora: 13.6\n176\t  result_rationale: 'PAR router 利用 Phase 0 已验证的 layer 6 激活信号（F1=0.993）进行软路由， routing\n177\t    diagonality 达到 0.92 意味着 92% 的权重正确分配给目标专家。 剩余 8% 的\"泄漏\"实际上是有益的： (1) 部分扰动（如 background\n178\t    clutter + 轻微 layout shift 同时出现）需要混合校正； (2) soft routing 的平滑梯度使得 PAR 在 E2E fine-tuning\n179\t    中可以学到比 hard routing  更精细的权重配置。 整体 78.4% 低于各专家在 own-type 上的最优成绩的加权平均（~81%），差距来源：\n180\t    (a) 8% 路由泄漏导致部分样本获得次优校正； (b) PAR fine-tuning 只调路由权重、冻结 LoRA，整体达不到联合训练的上界。 但 78.4%\n181\t    已经比 universal LoRA 高 13.6%，证明路由带来的专家选择增益远超路由误差成本。 layout 和 robot 达到 88% 和 86%（接近\n182\t    oracle 的 plan_002 数据），因为这两类是  单一子类型、PAR 分类难度最低。Visual 子类型（camera 72%、noise 70%）相对低一些，\n183\t    因为 4 种视觉扰动之间存在一定混淆（noise vs camera 的 PAR 权重偶尔偏移）。\n184\t\n185\t    '\n186\t  tables:\n187\t  - name: Meta-Brain per-perturbation breakdown\n188\t    columns:\n189\t    - Perturbation\n190\t    - Frozen\n191\t    - Universal\n192\t    - Meta-Brain\n193\t    - Gain vs Frozen\n194\t    - Gain vs Universal\n195\t    rows:\n196\t    - - camera\n197\t      - 42.0\n198\t      - 54.0\n199\t      - 72.0\n200\t      - '+30.0'\n201\t      - '+18.0'\n202\t    - - light\n203\t      - 58.0\n204\t      - 66.0\n205\t      - 78.0\n206\t      - '+20.0'\n207\t      - '+12.0'\n208\t    - - background\n209\t      - 52.0\n210\t      - 62.0\n211\t      - 76.0\n212\t      - '+24.0'\n213\t      - '+14.0'\n214\t    - - noise\n215\t      - 46.0\n216\t      - 54.0\n217\t      - 70.0\n218\t      - '+24.0'\n219\t      - '+16.0'\n220\t    - - layout\n221\t      - 68.0\n222\t      - 78.0\n223\t      - 88.0\n224\t      - '+20.0'\n225\t      - '+10.0'\n226\t    - - robot\n227\t      - 56.0\n228\t      - 74.0\n229\t      - 86.0\n230\t      - '+30.0'\n231\t      - '+12.0'\n232\t    - - Overall\n233\t      - 53.6\n234\t      - 64.8\n235\t      - 78.4\n236\t      - '+24.8'\n237\t      - '+13.6'\n238\t  figures_description:\n239\t  - 'Architecture diagram: Frozen pi0 → PaliGemma layer 6 → PAR MLP → [p_V, p_S, p_P]\n240\t    soft weights → LoRA-V/S/P bank → h_corrected = h_frozen + Σ p_k·LoRA_k(h). Only\n241\t    PAR weights are trainable (48K params), LoRA experts frozen from plan_002.'\n242\t  - 'Routing weight heatmap: 3×3 matrix (perturbation category × expert), near-diagonal\n243\t    with 0.91-0.93 on diagonal, 0.03-0.05 off-diagonal. Color-coded to show PAR correctly\n244\t    identifies perturbation type.'\n245\t  - 'Per-perturbation grouped bar chart: 6 clusters (one per type), 3 bars each (frozen/universal/meta-brain),\n246\t    showing consistent improvement across all types.'\n247\t  analysis: '13.6% gain over universal LoRA 是 Claim 2 的核心数值。在参数量相同（6M = 3×2M  vs 1×2M\n248\t    + 相同总 rank budget 的另一种分配）甚至 Meta-Brain 用了 3 倍参数的情况下， 关键洞察不是「更多参数 = 更好」而是「路由后的容量利用率远高于混合训练」。\n249\t    可做公平对比：rank-48 universal LoRA（与 3×rank-16 参数量相当）预期仍然饱和在 ~67%， 因为高 rank 并不能解决梯度冲突——这是\n250\t    plan_005 ablation ladder 要验证的。\n251\t\n252\t    '\n253\t- name: Oracle routing ablation\n254\t  plan_id: plan_004\n255\t  description: 'Replace PAR with ground-truth perturbation labels for hard routing.  Measures\n256\t    upper bound for routing quality.\n257\t\n258\t    '\n259\t  expected_results:\n260\t    oracle_overall: 79.6\n261\t    oracle_camera: 74.0\n262\t    oracle_light: 78.0\n263\t    oracle_background: 78.0\n264\t    oracle_noise: 72.0\n265\t    oracle_layout: 88.0\n266\t    oracle_robot: 88.0\n267\t    oracle_par_gap: 1.2\n268\t    oracle_par_gap_camera: 2.0\n269\t    oracle_par_gap_light: 0.0\n270\t    oracle_par_gap_background: 2.0\n271\t    oracle_par_gap_noise: 2.0\n272\t    oracle_par_gap_layout: 0.0\n273\t    oracle_par_gap_robot: 2.0\n274\t  result_rationale: 'Oracle-PAR gap 仅 1.2%，直接证明 Phase 0 的分类信号在下游任务中是 actionable 的。\n275\t    Gap 主要来自 Visual 子类型（camera +2, background +2, noise +2），因为 PAR 在  4 种 Visual 子类型间存在少量混淆（~8%\n276\t    路由泄漏），导致部分 Visual 样本获得了  LoRA-S/P 的轻微干扰。Layout 和 robot 的 gap 为 0-2%，因为这两类在 Phase\n277\t    0  的分类准确率接近 100%（单一子类型、特征空间高度分离）。 1.2% gap 远小于 Meta-Brain vs Universal LoRA 的\n278\t    13.6% gain，这意味着即使路由  有少量误差，路由策略本身的收益也远大于误差带来的损失。 Oracle 79.6% 低于各专家 own-type 最优的简单加权平均（~81%），因为\n279\t    oracle routing  是 hard routing（1-hot 权重），丢失了 soft routing 在某些混合扰动样本上的  blending\n280\t    优势。这也解释了为什么 PAR 的 soft routing 在某些类型上能接近 oracle。\n281\t\n282\t    '\n283\t  tables:\n284\t  - name: Oracle vs PAR per-perturbation gap\n285\t    columns:\n286\t    - Perturbation\n287\t    - PAR\n288\t    - Oracle\n289\t    - Gap\n290\t    rows:\n291\t    - - camera\n292\t      - 72.0\n293\t      - 74.0\n294\t      - 2.0\n295\t    - - light\n296\t      - 78.0\n297\t      - 78.0\n298\t      - 0.0\n299\t    - - background\n300\t      - 76.0\n301\t      - 78.0\n302\t      - 2.0\n303\t    - - noise\n304\t      - 70.0\n305\t      - 72.0\n306\t      - 2.0\n307\t    - - layout\n308\t      - 88.0\n309\t      - 88.0\n310\t      - 0.0\n311\t    - - robot\n312\t      - 86.0\n313\t      - 88.0\n314\t      - 2.0\n315\t    - - Overall\n316\t      - 78.4\n317\t      - 79.6\n318\t      - 1.2\n319\t  figures_description:\n320\t  - 'Paired bar chart: PAR vs Oracle per perturbation type, gap annotations on top.\n321\t    Visual types show small consistent gaps; Spatial/Physical nearly identical.'\n322\t  analysis: '1.2% gap 是对 reviewer concern C1（「Phase 0 分类太简单，路由无用」）的最佳回应： 分类简单 ≠ 路由无价值。分类简单意味着路由几乎免费获得正确性（zero\n323\t    overhead）， 而 13.6% 的 gain over universal 证明路由的价值在于下游校正，不在路由本身的难度。 Oracle gap 小反而是优势——说明\n324\t    PAR 已经接近天花板，无需更复杂的路由器。\n325\t\n326\t    '\n327\t- name: Ablation ladder — Frozen → Universal → Meta-Brain → Oracle\n328\t  plan_id: plan_005\n329\t  description: 'Systematic comparison on LIBERO-Plus with 5 seeds. Core evidence for\n330\t    Claim 2.\n331\t\n332\t    '\n333\t  expected_results:\n334\t    frozen_mean: 53.6\n335\t    frozen_std: 1.4\n336\t    universal_mean: 64.8\n337\t    universal_std: 1.8\n338\t    meta_brain_mean: 78.4\n339\t    meta_brain_std: 1.6\n340\t    oracle_mean: 79.6\n341\t    oracle_std: 1.2\n342\t    gain_frozen_to_universal: 11.2\n343\t    gain_universal_to_meta_brain: 13.6\n344\t    gain_meta_brain_to_oracle: 1.2\n345\t    gain_frozen_to_meta_brain: 24.8\n346\t    p_value_universal_vs_meta_brain: 0.0003\n347\t    p_value_meta_brain_vs_oracle: 0.14\n348\t  result_rationale: '5-seed 统计验证下，ablation ladder 呈现清晰的三级阶梯： (1) Frozen→Universal\n349\t    (+11.2%): universal LoRA 提供了基础的扰动鲁棒性， 证明 PaliGemma 层的 LoRA adaptation 是有效的校正机制。标准差\n350\t    1.8% 较高， 因为 universal LoRA 在不同 seed 下对不同扰动类型的容量分配方式不稳定（ 有时偏重 visual、有时偏重 spatial），导致\n351\t    run-to-run 方差较大。 (2) Universal→Meta-Brain (+13.6%, p<0.001): 路由带来的增益甚至超过 universal\n352\t    LoRA  自身 over frozen 的增益，统计显著。这是 Claim 2 最强的证据——同样的 LoRA capacity， 路由后的利用效率比混合使用高出一倍以上。Meta-Brain\n353\t    的标准差 1.6% 低于 universal  的 1.8%，因为路由机制减少了容量分配的随机性。 (3) Meta-Brain→Oracle (+1.2%,\n354\t    p=0.14): 差异不显著，证明 PAR 路由已接近上界。 这一不显著结果本身就是积极信号——说明无需 oracle 标签，Phase 0 分类足矣。\n355\t\n356\t    '\n357\t  tables:\n358\t  - name: Ablation ladder summary (5 seeds)\n359\t    columns:\n360\t    - Method\n361\t    - Params\n362\t    - Overall ± std\n363\t    - Gain over Frozen\n364\t    - Gain over Prev. Step\n365\t    rows:\n366\t    - - Frozen pi0\n367\t      - '0'\n368\t      - 53.6 ± 1.4\n369\t      - —\n370\t      - —\n371\t    - - Universal LoRA (r16)\n372\t      - ~2M\n373\t      - 64.8 ± 1.8\n374\t      - '+11.2'\n375\t      - '+11.2'\n376\t    - - Meta-Brain (PAR+ALB)\n377\t      - ~6M\n378\t      - 78.4 ± 1.6\n379\t      - '+24.8'\n380\t      - '+13.6'\n381\t    - - Oracle routing\n382\t      - ~6M\n383\t      - 79.6 ± 1.2\n384\t      - '+26.0'\n385\t      - '+1.2'\n386\t  - name: Per-perturbation ablation (mean over 5 seeds)\n387\t    columns:\n388\t    - Perturbation\n389\t    - Frozen\n390\t    - Universal\n391\t    - Meta-Brain\n392\t    - Oracle\n393\t    rows:\n394\t    - - camera\n395\t      - 42.0\n396\t      - 54.0\n397\t      - 72.0\n398\t      - 74.0\n399\t    - - light\n400\t      - 58.0\n401\t      - 66.0\n402\t      - 78.0\n403\t      - 78.0\n404\t    - - background\n405\t      - 52.0\n406\t      - 62.0\n407\t      - 76.0\n408\t      - 78.0\n409\t    - - noise\n410\t      - 46.0\n411\t      - 54.0\n412\t      - 70.0\n413\t      - 72.0\n414\t    - - layout\n415\t      - 68.0\n416\t      - 78.0\n417\t      - 88.0\n418\t      - 88.0\n419\t    - - robot\n420\t      - 56.0\n421\t      - 74.0\n422\t      - 86.0\n423\t      - 88.0\n424\t    - - Overall\n425\t      - 53.6\n426\t      - 64.8\n427\t      - 78.4\n428\t      - 79.6\n429\t  figures_description:\n430\t  - 'Bar chart (Figure 4 in paper): 4 bars per perturbation type + overall, ascending\n431\t    Frozen→Universal→Meta-Brain→Oracle. Error bars from 5 seeds. Clear staircase pattern;\n432\t    biggest jump is Universal→Meta-Brain.'\n433\t  - 'Delta decomposition stacked bar: overall gain 26.0% (oracle over frozen) decomposed\n434\t    into universal contribution (11.2), routing contribution (13.6), routing-perfection\n435\t    headroom (1.2).'\n436\t  analysis: 'Ablation ladder 的核心叙事：从 frozen 到 oracle 的 26.0% 总增益中， routing 贡献了 13.6%（52%），universal\n437\t    adaptation 贡献了 11.2%（43%）， routing 精度 headroom 仅 1.2%（5%）。这意味着 perturbation-diagnostic\n438\t    routing  不是边际优化，而是与 LoRA adaptation 本身同等量级的增益来源。 统计显著性分析确认 universal→meta-brain\n439\t    的增益是 robust 的（p<0.001）， 而 meta-brain→oracle 的差异不显著（p=0.14），为 PAR 路由的实用性提供了严格支持。\n440\t\n441\t    '\n442\t- name: FTM/FLA reproduction on pi0\n443\t  plan_id: plan_006\n444\t  description: 'Reproduce FTM on pi0 for visual perturbations. Compare with Meta-Brain\n445\t    on visual  and demonstrate Meta-Brain''s advantage on non-visual types.\n446\t\n447\t    '\n448\t  expected_results:\n449\t    ftm_camera: 70.0\n450\t    ftm_light: 76.0\n451\t    ftm_background: 72.0\n452\t    ftm_noise: 68.0\n453\t    ftm_visual_avg: 71.5\n454\t    ftm_layout: 68.0\n455\t    ftm_robot: 56.0\n456\t    ftm_overall: 68.3\n457\t    ftm_params_K: 4\n458\t    meta_brain_visual_avg: 74.0\n459\t    meta_brain_advantage_visual: 2.5\n460\t    meta_brain_advantage_overall: 10.1\n461\t    meta_brain_advantage_non_visual: 22.0\n462\t  result_rationale: 'FTM 在 pi0 上的复现结果合理偏低于原论文（原论文用不同 backbone 且只报告视觉扰动）。 FTM 在 visual\n463\t    子类型上达 71.5%（接近 LoRA-V 的 76.0%），说明 FTM 的 feature  modulation 策略确实能有效修复视觉损坏——这与\n464\t    FTM 原论文的结论一致。 但 FTM 在 layout (68.0%) 和 robot (56.0%) 上几乎无增益或低于 universal LoRA，\n465\t    因为 FTM 的设计假设扰动仅存在于视觉通道，其 modulation 无法处理空间关系和物理属性的变化。 Meta-Brain 在 visual 上略优于\n466\t    FTM (+2.5%)，因为 LoRA-V 有更多参数（2M vs 4K） 可以学到更精细的校正。关键差异在非 visual 类型：Meta-Brain 在\n467\t    layout+robot 上 平均 87.0% vs FTM 的 62.0%（+25.0%），这 25% 的差距直接论证了多类型校正的必要性。 FTM 的\n468\t    4K 参数量在 per-param visual gain 上极其高效，但 scope-limited—— 这在 parameter efficiency\n469\t    scatter plot (plan_007) 中会成为一个有趣的数据点。\n470\t\n471\t    '\n472\t  tables:\n473\t  - name: FTM vs Meta-Brain comparison\n474\t    columns:\n475\t    - Perturbation\n476\t    - FTM (4K)\n477\t    - Meta-Brain (6M)\n478\t    - LoRA-V (2M)\n479\t    - Universal (2M)\n480\t    rows:\n481\t    - - camera\n482\t      - 70.0\n483\t      - 72.0\n484\t      - 74.0\n485\t      - 54.0\n486\t    - - light\n487\t      - 76.0\n488\t      - 78.0\n489\t      - 80.0\n490\t      - 66.0\n491\t    - - background\n492\t      - 72.0\n493\t      - 76.0\n494\t      - 78.0\n495\t      - 62.0\n496\t    - - noise\n497\t      - 68.0\n498\t      - 70.0\n499\t      - 72.0\n500\t      - 54.0\n501\t    - - layout\n502\t      - 68.0\n503\t      - 88.0\n504\t      - 60.0\n505\t      - 78.0\n506\t    - - robot\n507\t      - 56.0\n508\t      - 86.0\n509\t      - 54.0\n510\t      - 74.0\n511\t    - - Overall\n512\t      - 68.3\n513\t      - 78.4\n514\t      - 69.7\n515\t      - 64.8\n516\t  figures_description:\n517\t  - 'Radar chart: 6 axes (perturbation types), overlaid polygons for FTM/Meta-Brain/Universal.\n518\t    FTM polygon inflated in left 4 axes (visual) but deflated in right 2 (spatial/physical);\n519\t    Meta-Brain polygon uniformly large.'\n520\t  analysis: 'FTM 是一个重要的 baseline，因为它代表了「单模态专家」的最佳案例。 Meta-Brain 的价值主张不是在任何单一类型上打败\n521\t    FTM，而是在所有类型上同时提供  强大校正——这正是 perturbation-diagnostic routing 的设计目标。 在论文中应将 FTM\n522\t    定位为「visual-only routing 的上界参考」， 并强调 Meta-Brain 的 multi-type coverage 是其独特贡献。\n523\t\n524\t    '\n525\t- name: Parameter efficiency analysis\n526\t  plan_id: plan_007\n527\t  description: 'Compute gain-over-frozen per method, normalize by trainable params.  Generate\n528\t    scatter plot (x=params, y=gain). Core visual evidence for Claim 3.\n529\t\n530\t    '\n531\t  expected_results:\n532\t    meta_brain_gain: 24.8\n533\t    meta_brain_params_M: 6.1\n534\t    meta_brain_gain_per_M: 4.07\n535\t    meta_brain_with_cm_gain: 27.2\n536\t    meta_brain_with_cm_params_M: 6.1\n537\t    meta_brain_with_cm_gain_per_M: 4.46\n538\t    universal_lora_gain: 11.2\n539\t    universal_lora_params_M: 2.0\n540\t    universal_lora_gain_per_M: 5.6\n541\t    ftm_gain_overall: 14.7\n542\t    ftm_params_M: 0.004\n543\t    ftm_gain_per_M: 3675.0\n544\t    vla_gse_gain: 27.6\n545\t    vla_gse_params_M: 114.0\n546\t    vla_gse_gain_per_M: 0.24\n547\t    meta_brain_vs_vla_gse_param_ratio: 18.7\n548\t    meta_brain_vs_vla_gse_gain_ratio: 0.9\n549\t    meta_brain_pareto_optimal: true\n550\t  result_rationale: 'Meta-Brain 的 gain/M-param = 4.07，是 VLA-GSE (0.24) 的 17 倍。 在 scatter\n551\t    plot 上 Meta-Brain 位于 Pareto 前沿的关键位置： (1) 相比 VLA-GSE：以 5.3% 的参数量达到 90% 的 gain，参数效率高\n552\t    17x； (2) 相比 Universal LoRA：gain/M 虽低（4.07 vs 5.60），但绝对 gain 高 13.6%， 说明 3x 参数扩展用于路由（而非增大\n553\t    rank）是高效的； (3) 相比 FTM：FTM 的 per-param efficiency 极高（3675 gain/M）但绝对 gain  受限于\n554\t    visual-only scope，在 scatter plot 上位于右下角「高效率低总量」区域。 这三对比较构成 Claim 3 的完整论证：Meta-Brain\n555\t    在「参数-增益」trade-off  空间中占据了 VLA-GSE 和 FTM 之间的最优区间。 VLA-GSE 的 gain 数据直接引自原论文（Qwen3-VL-4B\n556\t    backbone 上 frozen 53.6%→81.2%， gain=27.6%），跨 backbone 比较需在论文中注明 caveat。\n557\t\n558\t    '\n559\t  tables:\n560\t  - name: Parameter efficiency comparison\n561\t    columns:\n562\t    - Method\n563\t    - Backbone\n564\t    - Trainable Params\n565\t    - Gain over Frozen\n566\t    - Gain/M-param\n567\t    rows:\n568\t    - - FTM\n569\t      - pi0\n570\t      - 4K\n571\t      - 14.7\n572\t      - 3675.0\n573\t    - - Universal LoRA (r16)\n574\t      - pi0\n575\t      - 2.0M\n576\t      - 11.2\n577\t      - 5.6\n578\t    - - Meta-Brain\n579\t      - pi0\n580\t      - 6.1M\n581\t      - 24.8\n582\t      - 4.07\n583\t    - - Meta-Brain + CM\n584\t      - pi0\n585\t      - 6.1M\n586\t      - 27.2\n587\t      - 4.46\n588\t    - - VLA-GSE*\n589\t      - Qwen3-VL-4B\n590\t      - 114M\n591\t      - 27.6\n592\t      - 0.24\n593\t  figures_description:\n594\t  - 'Scatter plot (Figure 5 in paper): x-axis = trainable params (log scale, 1K to\n595\t    200M), y-axis = gain over frozen baseline (%). Points: FTM (bottom-left, high\n596\t    slope from origin), Universal LoRA (mid-left), Meta-Brain (mid, star marker),\n597\t    Meta-Brain+CM (mid, diamond), VLA-GSE (far right, asterisk with cross-backbone\n598\t    caveat). Pareto front line through FTM→Meta-Brain→VLA-GSE. Meta-Brain clearly\n599\t    on or near Pareto front. Dashed iso-efficiency lines (constant gain/M) for reference.'\n600\t  analysis: 'Scatter plot 是 Claim 3 的视觉锚点。关键信息：在 log-scale x 轴上， Meta-Brain 距 VLA-GSE\n601\t    向左一个数量级以上，但 y 轴差距很小（24.8 vs 27.6）。 论文应在图注中明确 VLA-GSE 使用不同 backbone（Qwen3-VL-4B），\n602\t    并引导读者关注 gain-over-own-baseline 指标而非绝对值。 Universal LoRA 的数据点是重要的 in-backbone 参照——它证明仅增加参数（从\n603\t    2M 到 6M） 不如增加路由（从 universal 到 routed），因为 rank-48 universal LoRA 预期仍 ~67%。\n604\t\n605\t    '\n606\t- name: Correction Memory ablation\n607\t  plan_id: plan_008\n608\t  description: 'Compare Meta-Brain with and without Correction Memory. CM modulates\n609\t    routing  weights via retrieved exemplars. Quantify marginal gain.\n610\t\n611\t    '\n612\t  expected_results:\n613\t    meta_brain_no_cm: 78.4\n614\t    meta_brain_with_cm: 80.8\n615\t    cm_ablation_delta: 2.4\n616\t    cm_delta_camera: 2.0\n617\t    cm_delta_light: 2.0\n618\t    cm_delta_background: 2.0\n619\t    cm_delta_noise: 4.0\n620\t    cm_delta_layout: 2.0\n621\t    cm_delta_robot: 3.0\n622\t    cm_alpha_learned: 0.18\n623\t    cm_retrieval_latency_ms: 0.8\n624\t    cm_faiss_index_size_MB: 12\n625\t  result_rationale: 'CM 的 2.4% 增益来自两个机制： (1) 路由权重精修：对于 PAR 不确定的样本（routing entropy\n626\t    较高）， CM 从 FAISS 检索到的 k-NN exemplar 提供了基于历史成功案例的权重校准， 将这些 borderline 样本推向正确专家。noise\n627\t    类型获益最大（+4.0%）， 因为 sensor_noise 与 camera 扰动在激活空间中距离较近，PAR 在此区域 routing 不确定性最高，CM\n628\t    的 exemplar matching 恰好能消除这一歧义。 (2) 校正强度调制：learned alpha=0.18 说明 CM 的权重修正幅度温和，\n629\t    不会覆盖 PAR 的主信号，仅在需要时提供微调——这是「optional module」 定位的实验支撑。 CM 只增加 1 个可学习参数（alpha）+\n630\t    CPU-bound FAISS 检索（0.8ms）， 对推理延迟几乎无影响，使其成为一个低风险的即插即用模块。 2.4% gain 在 [1, 4] 范围内，足以在论文中报告但不构成核心贡献——\n631\t    这恰好是理想定位：CM 是额外加分项而非系统必要组件。\n632\t\n633\t    '\n634\t  tables:\n635\t  - name: CM ablation per-perturbation\n636\t    columns:\n637\t    - Perturbation\n638\t    - w/o CM\n639\t    - w/ CM\n640\t    - CM Delta\n641\t    rows:\n642\t    - - camera\n643\t      - 72.0\n644\t      - 74.0\n645\t      - '+2.0'\n646\t    - - light\n647\t      - 78.0\n648\t      - 80.0\n649\t      - '+2.0'\n650\t    - - background\n651\t      - 76.0\n652\t      - 78.0\n653\t      - '+2.0'\n654\t    - - noise\n655\t      - 70.0\n656\t      - 74.0\n657\t      - '+4.0'\n658\t    - - layout\n659\t      - 88.0\n660\t      - 90.0\n661\t      - '+2.0'\n662\t    - - robot\n663\t      - 86.0\n664\t      - 89.0\n665\t      - '+3.0'\n666\t    - - Overall\n667\t      - 78.4\n668\t      - 80.8\n669\t      - '+2.4'\n670\t  figures_description:\n671\t  - 'Paired bar chart: w/ and w/o CM for each perturbation type. CM gains highlighted\n672\t    with delta annotations. Noise and robot types show largest improvements.'\n673\t  - 'Scatter: per-sample routing entropy (x) vs CM-induced weight change magnitude\n674\t    (y), showing CM intervenes most on high-entropy (uncertain) samples.'\n675\t  analysis: 'CM 对 reviewer concern C6 的回应很清晰：2.4% gain with 1 learned param,  0.8ms\n676\t    latency, 完全 optional。建议在论文中将 CM 放在 ablation section 而非  main method，避免给审稿人造成「系统过于复杂」的印象。\n677\t    noise 类型的 +4% 增益可以作为 case study 展示 CM 的工作机制。\n678\t\n679\t    '\n680\t- name: Router architecture comparison\n681\t  plan_id: plan_009\n682\t  description: 'Compare PAR router variants: 2-layer MLP, linear classifier, attention-based.  All\n683\t    on PaliGemma layer 6. Measure routing accuracy and downstream success.\n684\t\n685\t    '\n686\t  expected_results:\n687\t    mlp_routing_acc: 97.2\n688\t    mlp_downstream: 78.4\n689\t    mlp_params_K: 48\n690\t    linear_routing_acc: 94.1\n691\t    linear_downstream: 76.6\n692\t    linear_params_K: 6\n693\t    attention_routing_acc: 97.8\n694\t    attention_downstream: 78.8\n695\t    attention_params_K: 196\n696\t    mlp_vs_linear_downstream_gap: 1.8\n697\t    mlp_vs_attention_downstream_gap: -0.4\n698\t  result_rationale: '三种路由器的性能梯度与 Phase 0 的分类难度分析一致： (1) Linear (94.1% → 76.6%): 线性可分性已经很强（Phase\n699\t    0 证实 layer 6 的类别边界 几乎线性），但 ~6% 的误差集中在 Visual 子类型间的边界区域（noise vs camera）， 导致下游\n700\t    1.8% 的性能损失。线性模型只有 6K params，极其轻量。 (2) MLP (97.2% → 78.4%): 两层 MLP 捕捉到非线性边界，将路由误差压缩到\n701\t    2.8%， 在参数效率（48K）和性能间取得最佳平衡。48K 相对于 6M LoRA params 可忽略不计。 (3) Attention (97.8%\n702\t    → 78.8%): attention 机制可以利用 token 间关系进行路由， 略优于 MLP (+0.6% routing, +0.4% downstream)，但参数量增加\n703\t    4x（196K）， 增益不具统计显著性。 MLP 是论文默认选择的合理性得到验证：比 linear 明显好、与 attention 实质等价、 参数最经济。\n704\t\n705\t    '\n706\t  tables:\n707\t  - name: Router architecture comparison\n708\t    columns:\n709\t    - Router\n710\t    - Params\n711\t    - Routing Acc (%)\n712\t    - Downstream (%)\n713\t    - Δ vs MLP\n714\t    rows:\n715\t    - - Linear\n716\t      - 6K\n717\t      - 94.1\n718\t      - 76.6\n719\t      - '-1.8'\n720\t    - - 2-layer MLP (default)\n721\t      - 48K\n722\t      - 97.2\n723\t      - 78.4\n724\t      - —\n725\t    - - Attention-based\n726\t      - 196K\n727\t      - 97.8\n728\t      - 78.8\n729\t      - '+0.4'\n730\t  figures_description:\n731\t  - 'Small dual-axis bar chart: routing accuracy (left axis) and downstream success\n732\t    (right axis) for 3 router types. Shows diminishing returns beyond MLP.'\n733\t  analysis: '这个实验回答了一个隐含问题：路由器复杂度如何影响整体系统？ 答案是：影响极小。94.1→97.2% 的路由精度提升带来 1.8% 下游增益，\n734\t    但 97.2→97.8% 的进一步提升仅带来 0.4%。这是因为 Phase 0 分类本身很容易， 简单模型已足够——与 reviewer concern\n735\t    C1 的回应一致。 建议在 appendix 报告此结果，主文只提 MLP 作为默认配置。\n736\t\n737\t    '\n738\t- name: 6-class vs 3-class routing comparison\n739\t  plan_id: plan_010\n740\t  description: 'Compare 6-class fine-grained routing (6 LoRA experts) vs 3-class coarse\n741\t    routing  (3 experts). Test whether finer granularity justifies additional parameters.\n742\t\n743\t    '\n744\t  expected_results:\n745\t    three_class_overall: 78.4\n746\t    three_class_params_M: 6.1\n747\t    six_class_overall: 79.4\n748\t    six_class_params_M: 12.2\n749\t    marginal_gain: 1.0\n750\t    marginal_gain_per_additional_expert: 0.33\n751\t    six_class_camera: 74.0\n752\t    six_class_light: 80.0\n753\t    six_class_background: 78.0\n754\t    six_class_noise: 74.0\n755\t    six_class_layout: 88.0\n756\t    six_class_robot: 82.0\n757\t    six_class_routing_acc: 96.8\n758\t    intra_visual_gain: 1.5\n759\t    spatial_physical_gain: -0.7\n760\t  result_rationale: '6-class routing 仅带来 1.0% 的边际增益，原因： (1) Phase 0 已显示 intra-Visual\n761\t    子类型之间的特征距离远小于 inter-category 距离， 6-class 在 Visual 子类型间的路由精度（96.8%）略低于 3-class（97.2%），\n762\t    说明更细的边界带来了更多的路由噪声； (2) Visual 子类型的校正模式确实有差异（camera 需要修复 color/geometry 畸变， noise\n763\t    需要去噪平滑），所以 6 个专家在 Visual 上略优 (+1.5%)， 但这一增益被 spatial/physical 的轻微退化 (-0.7%) 部分抵消——\n764\t    6-class 中 layout 和 robot 各自只有一个专家（与 3-class 相同）， 但 router 增加了 4 个 Visual 类别输出后\n765\t    softmax 分母增大， 导致 layout/robot 的 routing confidence 略降； (3) 6 个 LoRA 专家的参数量翻倍（12.2M），但增益仅\n766\t    1.0%， gain/additional-param 极低（0.33%/expert vs 3-class 的 4.07 gain/M）。 结论：3-class\n767\t    taxonomy 在效率-性能 trade-off 上是最优粒度， 与 Phase 0 的 mechanistic 分析（early/mid/late layers\n768\t    对应 Visual/Spatial/Physical）一致。\n769\t\n770\t    '\n771\t  tables:\n772\t  - name: 6-class vs 3-class per-perturbation\n773\t    columns:\n774\t    - Perturbation\n775\t    - 3-class\n776\t    - 6-class\n777\t    - Delta\n778\t    rows:\n779\t    - - camera\n780\t      - 72.0\n781\t      - 74.0\n782\t      - '+2.0'\n783\t    - - light\n784\t      - 78.0\n785\t      - 80.0\n786\t      - '+2.0'\n787\t    - - background\n788\t      - 76.0\n789\t      - 78.0\n790\t      - '+2.0'\n791\t    - - noise\n792\t      - 70.0\n793\t      - 74.0\n794\t      - '+4.0'\n795\t    - - layout\n796\t      - 88.0\n797\t      - 88.0\n798\t      - '0.0'\n799\t    - - robot\n800\t      - 86.0\n801\t      - 82.0\n802\t      - '-4.0'\n803\t    - - Overall\n804\t      - 78.4\n805\t      - 79.4\n806\t      - '+1.0'\n807\t  figures_description:\n808\t  - 'Grouped bar chart: 3-class vs 6-class per type. Visual types show small gains;\n809\t    robot shows slight regression. Annotations: total param cost for each configuration.'\n810\t  analysis: '这个结果直接回应 reviewer concern C5（3-class 是否太粗）： 答案是「对当前任务集合，3-class 是 sweet\n811\t    spot」。论文应在 discussion 中  承认 6-class 在某些 Visual 子类型上有额外区分度，但将 3-class 定位为  Occam''s\n812\t    razor 选择。robot 类的 -4% 退化值得关注——可能是因为 6 个 softmax  输出中 robot 的 prior probability\n813\t    被稀释。如果 LIBERO-Plus 扩展更多物理扰动 子类型，6-class 或更细的 taxonomy 可能变得必要。\n814\t\n815\t    '\n816\t- name: Cross-backbone validation — OpenVLA\n817\t  plan_id: plan_011\n818\t  description: 'Replicate Phase 0 + Phase 1 core pipeline on OpenVLA to test generalizability  of\n819\t    perturbation-diagnostic routing across architectures.\n820\t\n821\t    '\n822\t  expected_results:\n823\t    cross_backbone: OpenVLA (SigLIP + Llama-2-7B)\n824\t    phase0_3class_f1: 0.972\n825\t    phase0_best_layer: 8\n826\t    phase0_pooling: mean\n827\t    openvla_frozen_overall: 48.2\n828\t    openvla_universal_lora_overall: 58.6\n829\t    openvla_meta_brain_overall: 70.4\n830\t    openvla_gain_over_frozen: 22.2\n831\t    openvla_gain_over_universal: 11.8\n832\t    openvla_oracle_overall: 71.8\n833\t    openvla_oracle_par_gap: 1.4\n834\t    openvla_routing_diagonality: 0.89\n835\t  result_rationale: 'OpenVLA 上的复现确认 perturbation-diagnostic routing 是跨架构通用的： (1) Phase\n836\t    0 F1=0.972（略低于 pi0 的 0.993）：OpenVLA 使用 SigLIP（非 PaliGemma） 作为视觉编码器，最佳层从 layer\n837\t    6 移至 layer 8，但分类精度依然极高。 这与 SAFE 论文在 OpenVLA 上的 probing 结果一致，进一步支持「VLA 内部表征  普遍编码扰动类型信息」的核心假说。\n838\t    (2) gain over frozen = 22.2%（pi0 上为 24.8%）：绝对增益略低，因为 OpenVLA  的 frozen baseline\n839\t    更低（48.2% vs 53.6%），说明 OpenVLA 本身对扰动更脆弱， 校正难度更大。但 gain 仍在 best-tier 范围 [22, 28]\n840\t    的低端。 (3) gain over universal = 11.8%（pi0 上为 13.6%）：路由增益在 OpenVLA 上  同样显著，确认了 Claim\n841\t    2 的跨架构有效性。 (4) Oracle-PAR gap = 1.4%（pi0 上为 1.2%）：略大但仍在 [0, 2] 内， 与 Phase 0 F1\n842\t    略低（0.972 vs 0.993）一致。 OpenVLA 的较低绝对性能可归因于其较小的视觉编码器容量和不同的训练数据分布。\n843\t\n844\t    '\n845\t  tables:\n846\t  - name: Cross-backbone comparison\n847\t    columns:\n848\t    - Metric\n849\t    - pi0 (PaliGemma)\n850\t    - OpenVLA (SigLIP)\n851\t    rows:\n852\t    - - Phase 0 3-class F1\n853\t      - 0.993\n854\t      - 0.972\n855\t    - - Best probe layer\n856\t      - 6\n857\t      - 8\n858\t    - - Frozen baseline (%)\n859\t      - 53.6\n860\t      - 48.2\n861\t    - - Universal LoRA (%)\n862\t      - 64.8\n863\t      - 58.6\n864\t    - - Meta-Brain (%)\n865\t      - 78.4\n866\t      - 70.4\n867\t    - - Oracle (%)\n868\t      - 79.6\n869\t      - 71.8\n870\t    - - Gain over frozen\n871\t      - 24.8\n872\t      - 22.2\n873\t    - - Gain over universal\n874\t      - 13.6\n875\t      - 11.8\n876\t    - - Oracle-PAR gap\n877\t      - 1.2\n878\t      - 1.4\n879\t    - - Routing diagonality\n880\t      - 0.92\n881\t      - 0.89\n882\t  figures_description:\n883\t  - Side-by-side ablation ladder bars for pi0 and OpenVLA, showing parallel staircase\n884\t    pattern despite different absolute values. Gain-over-frozen annotations highlight\n885\t    comparable relative improvements.\n886\t  analysis: '跨 backbone 验证是应对 reviewer concern C3 的关键实验。 尽管绝对数值不同（OpenVLA 整体低 ~8%），增益模式高度一致：\n887\t    universal→meta-brain 的 gain 在两个 backbone 上分别为 13.6% 和 11.8%， routing diagonality\n888\t    分别为 0.92 和 0.89——都远高于 random baseline (0.33)。 Phase 0 的最佳层从 layer 6 (PaliGemma)\n889\t    移至 layer 8 (SigLIP) 符合预期： 不同视觉编码器的信息编码深度不同，但扰动类型信息的可提取性是通用的。 论文中应以 gain-over-baseline\n890\t    为主要比较指标，避免直接对比绝对值。\n891\t\n892\t    '\n893\t- name: LoRA layer placement ablation\n894\t  plan_id: plan_012\n895\t  description: 'Vary which PaliGemma layers receive LoRA. Test whether optimal layer\n896\t    placement  differs by perturbation type (early for Visual, mid for Spatial, late\n897\t    for Physical).\n898\t\n899\t    '\n900\t  expected_results:\n901\t    lora_v_early_2_8: 77.2\n902\t    lora_v_mid_6_12: 72.8\n903\t    lora_v_late_12_18: 68.4\n904\t    lora_v_all: 76.0\n905\t    lora_s_early_2_8: 82.0\n906\t    lora_s_mid_6_12: 91.4\n907\t    lora_s_late_12_18: 86.0\n908\t    lora_s_all: 90.0\n909\t    lora_p_early_2_8: 78.0\n910\t    lora_p_mid_6_12: 82.0\n911\t    lora_p_late_12_18: 89.2\n912\t    lora_p_all: 88.0\n913\t    optimal_v: early (layers 2-8)\n914\t    optimal_s: mid (layers 6-12)\n915\t    optimal_p: late (layers 12-18)\n916\t    type_aligned_overall: 80.2\n917\t    all_layers_overall: 78.4\n918\t    type_aligned_gain_over_all_layers: 1.8\n919\t  result_rationale: '层放置的最优分布与 VLA 处理扰动的 mechanistic 假设高度吻合： (1) LoRA-V 最优在 early\n920\t    layers (2-8): Visual 扰动（camera/light/background/noise） 在视觉编码阶段损坏表征，early layers\n921\t    是信号最先被破坏的地方， 在此处施加 LoRA 校正效率最高。LoRA-V 在 late layers 仅 68.4%（接近 universal LoRA），\n922\t    因为视觉损坏在传播到高层后已经耦合到语义表征中，难以局部修复。 (2) LoRA-S 最优在 mid layers (6-12): Spatial 扰动改变物体空间关系，\n923\t    这类信息在 mid layers 被编码为 spatial token relationships。 LoRA-S 在 mid layers 达 91.4%（超过\n924\t    all-layers 的 90.0%）， 说明集中校正比分散校正更有效——避免了 early/late layers 的无用更新。 (3) LoRA-P 最优在\n925\t    late layers (12-18): Physical 扰动影响动力学属性， 这些信息在高层被整合为 action planning 信号。LoRA-P\n926\t    在 late layers 达 89.2%。 Type-aligned 配置（每个专家放在最优层区间）比 all-layers 配置高 1.8%， 同时每个专家的参数量减少\n927\t    ~60%（仅覆盖 6 层而非 18 层）。 这为更极致的参数效率提供了方向，但增加了系统复杂度。\n928\t\n929\t    '\n930\t  tables:\n931\t  - name: Layer placement × expert type (own-type success rate %)\n932\t    columns:\n933\t    - Expert\n934\t    - Early (2-8)\n935\t    - Mid (6-12)\n936\t    - Late (12-18)\n937\t    - All layers\n938\t    rows:\n939\t    - - LoRA-V (Visual)\n940\t      - 77.2\n941\t      - 72.8\n942\t      - 68.4\n943\t      - 76.0\n944\t    - - LoRA-S (Spatial)\n945\t      - 82.0\n946\t      - 91.4\n947\t      - 86.0\n948\t      - 90.0\n949\t    - - LoRA-P (Physical)\n950\t      - 78.0\n951\t      - 82.0\n952\t      - 89.2\n953\t      - 88.0\n954\t  - name: System-level layer placement comparison\n955\t    columns:\n956\t    - Configuration\n957\t    - Params/expert\n958\t    - Visual\n959\t    - Spatial\n960\t    - Physical\n961\t    - Overall\n962\t    rows:\n963\t    - - All layers (default)\n964\t      - ~2.0M\n965\t      - 76.0\n966\t      - 90.0\n967\t      - 88.0\n968\t      - 78.4\n969\t    - - Type-aligned layers\n970\t      - ~0.8M\n971\t      - 77.2\n972\t      - 91.4\n973\t      - 89.2\n974\t      - 80.2\n975\t  figures_description:\n976\t  - '3×3 heatmap: expert rows × layer-group columns, cell values = own-type success\n977\t    rate. Clear diagonal pattern (V-early, S-mid, P-late) with highest values along\n978\t    the diagonal.'\n979\t  analysis: 层放置 ablation 提供了 mechanistic insight 而非直接的系统设计改进。 对角模式（V-early, S-mid,\n980\t    P-late）与 VLA 的分层信息处理模型一致， 为 Phase 0 的单层分类结果提供了因果方向的支持：layer 6 能区分扰动类型， 因为不同类型的信息损坏恰好在该层汇聚/分离。\n981\t    Type-aligned 配置带来 1.8% 增益和 60% 参数节省，但增加了工程复杂度 （需要为每个专家配置不同的层 mask）。建议在论文 appendix\n982\t    中作为  「进一步优化方向」报告，主系统保持 all-layers 的简洁配置。\n983\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01LQ4Te7gZVbHZuRYt6tuXWZ","session_id":"f3c89458-961d-4d5e-a388-373831b4983c","uuid":"3c9cb9a6-189e-4793-b6eb-c60fde0e42eb","timestamp":"2026-05-15T16:39:21.123Z"}
