{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01LQ4Te7gZVbHZuRYt6tuXWZ","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Review submitted. Here is the summary of the review:\n\n**Overall Rating: 6 (Borderline Accept) | Confidence: 4/5**\n\nThe review of the median-tier results for Meta-Brain (perturbation-diagnostic LoRA routing for VLAs) identifies:\n\n**Key strengths:**\n- Phase 0 finding (F1=0.993 single-layer perturbation classification) is the paper's strongest contribution\n- Clean ablation ladder with 5-seed statistics: all adjacent steps significant at p<0.05\n- Comprehensive experiment coverage (11 experiments) — unusual breadth\n- Cross-backbone validation on SmolVLA replicates the routing benefit pattern\n- Expert cross-evaluation matrix convincingly motivates routing as necessary, not optional\n\n**Key weaknesses:**\n- Spatial routing gain is negligible (+1.1%, captures only 25.6% of oracle ceiling) — undermines the 3-class coverage claim\n- **Missing parameter-matched universal LoRA baseline (rank-48, ~6M params)** — the most critical gap; without it, routing benefit cannot be separated from parameter scaling\n- VLA-GSE comparison is cross-backbone and therefore weak despite similar frozen baselines\n- Oracle-PAR gap of 3.9% (p=0.021) is non-trivial — 40% of routing potential left on the table\n- Correction Memory (+1.2%) is padding, not a meaningful contribution\n- Training data asymmetry across experts could confound expert quality differences\n\n**Blocking concerns for acceptance:** The rank-48 universal LoRA control and the random routing baseline. If the former confirms routing benefit beyond parameter scaling, the paper becomes a solid accept.\n\nThe review report was saved to `/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-be-idea-gen-0515/projects/meta_brain_lora_routing/artifacts/dream_reports/dream_20260515T154653/median/review_report.md`."},{"type":"text","text":"agentId: a2d7d90eefab01575 (use SendMessage with to: 'a2d7d90eefab01575' to continue this agent)\n<usage>total_tokens: 135211\ntool_uses: 20\nduration_ms: 141819</usage>"}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f3c89458-961d-4d5e-a388-373831b4983c","uuid":"e7afe814-8454-4a3a-b96d-314f4396b3fd","timestamp":"2026-05-15T16:41:01.654Z","tool_use_result":{"status":"completed","prompt":"You are Reviewer R1 for a CoRL 2026 submission. Your focus areas are **Methods** and **Experiments**.\n\n## CoRL Review Standards\n- **Venue**: CoRL (Conference on Robot Learning), acceptance rate ~30%\n- **Rating scale**: 1-10 (10=top 5% seminal, 8=strong accept, 6=weak accept/borderline accept, 5=borderline, 4=weak reject, 3=clear reject, 1=strong reject)\n- **Confidence**: 1-5 (5=absolutely certain, 4=confident, 3=fairly confident, 2=willing to defend, 1=educated guess)\n- **Evaluation dimensions**: Originality, Quality, Clarity, Significance, Relevance, Limitations\n- CoRL values: real robot experiments preferred but simulation accepted for architecture contributions; relevance to robot learning community; reproducibility\n\n## Paper Summary\n**Title**: Meta-Brain: Perturbation-Diagnostic LoRA Routing for Robust Vision-Language-Action Models\n\n**Core idea**: Frozen VLA activations encode perturbation type (Visual/Spatial/Physical) with near-perfect accuracy at a single layer. Meta-Brain exploits this by routing corrective LoRA experts via a lightweight Perturbation-Aware Router (PAR), achieving 71.4% on LIBERO-Plus with ~6M params (vs. 53.6% frozen, 65.4% universal LoRA, 75.3% oracle).\n\n**Architecture**:\n1. PAR: 2-layer MLP (~50K params) on frozen PaliGemma layer-6 mean-pooled hidden states → softmax over 3 classes\n2. ALB: 3 rank-16 LoRA adapters (Visual, Spatial, Physical), ~6M total\n3. Optional Correction Memory (CM): FAISS-indexed exemplar retrieval, learned alpha=0.23 blending\n\n**Key results**:\n- Ablation ladder: Frozen (53.6) < Universal (65.4) < Meta-Brain (71.4) < Oracle (75.3), all steps significant (p<0.05)\n- Routing gains asymmetric: Visual +8.7%, Physical +5.2%, Spatial +1.1% over universal\n- 64.5% of VLA-GSE's gain at 5.3% of params\n- Cross-backbone on SmolVLA: +5.6% over universal (comparable to pi0's +6.0%)\n- Layer placement ablation: V→early, S→mid, P→late peaks (crossed pattern)\n- 6-class vs 3-class: only +0.8% for 2× params\n- CM: +1.2% overall (marginal)\n- Router architecture: MLP best cost/performance tradeoff\n\n**Experiment design reference (from review_context.yaml)**:\nThe paper covers all 10 imagined experiments from the design document:\n1. Expert specialization cross-type matrix ✓\n2. Meta-Brain assembly + PAR routing ✓  \n3. Oracle routing upper bound ✓\n4. Ablation ladder with 5-seed statistics ✓\n5. FTM/FLA visual-only baseline comparison ✓\n6. Parameter efficiency analysis ✓\n7. CM ablation ✓\n8. Router architecture comparison ✓\n9. 6-class vs 3-class ✓\n10. Cross-backbone SmolVLA ✓\n11. Layer placement ablation ✓\n\n## Your Task\nProvide a detailed review focused on **Methods** and **Experiments**. Structure your review as:\n\n### 1. Summary (2-3 sentences)\n\n### 2. Strengths (bulleted, focus on method design and experimental rigor)\n\n### 3. Weaknesses (bulleted, focus on methodological gaps and experimental concerns)\n\n### 4. Questions for Authors\n\n### 5. Missing Experiments or Analyses\n\n### 6. Scores\n- Soundness (1-4): Is the method technically correct?\n- Empirical Rigor (1-4): Are experiments sufficient and well-controlled?\n- Reproducibility (1-4): Could someone reproduce this?\n- Overall Rating (1-10, CoRL scale)\n- Confidence (1-5)\n\nBe rigorous but fair. Pay special attention to:\n- Whether the 3-class perturbation taxonomy is well-justified or overly simplistic\n- Whether the \"frozen activations encode perturbation type\" claim is as novel/surprising as presented\n- The VLA-GSE comparison fairness (different backbone)\n- Whether spatial underperformance is adequately addressed or is a significant weakness\n- Statistical rigor (5 seeds, p-values, confidence intervals)\n- The gap between Meta-Brain and oracle (only 60.6% of ceiling captured)\n- Whether the Correction Memory module is a meaningful contribution or padding\n","agentId":"a2d7d90eefab01575","agentType":"general-purpose","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Review submitted. Here is the summary of the review:\n\n**Overall Rating: 6 (Borderline Accept) | Confidence: 4/5**\n\nThe review of the median-tier results for Meta-Brain (perturbation-diagnostic LoRA routing for VLAs) identifies:\n\n**Key strengths:**\n- Phase 0 finding (F1=0.993 single-layer perturbation classification) is the paper's strongest contribution\n- Clean ablation ladder with 5-seed statistics: all adjacent steps significant at p<0.05\n- Comprehensive experiment coverage (11 experiments) — unusual breadth\n- Cross-backbone validation on SmolVLA replicates the routing benefit pattern\n- Expert cross-evaluation matrix convincingly motivates routing as necessary, not optional\n\n**Key weaknesses:**\n- Spatial routing gain is negligible (+1.1%, captures only 25.6% of oracle ceiling) — undermines the 3-class coverage claim\n- **Missing parameter-matched universal LoRA baseline (rank-48, ~6M params)** — the most critical gap; without it, routing benefit cannot be separated from parameter scaling\n- VLA-GSE comparison is cross-backbone and therefore weak despite similar frozen baselines\n- Oracle-PAR gap of 3.9% (p=0.021) is non-trivial — 40% of routing potential left on the table\n- Correction Memory (+1.2%) is padding, not a meaningful contribution\n- Training data asymmetry across experts could confound expert quality differences\n\n**Blocking concerns for acceptance:** The rank-48 universal LoRA control and the random routing baseline. If the former confirms routing benefit beyond parameter scaling, the paper becomes a solid accept.\n\nThe review report was saved to `/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-be-idea-gen-0515/projects/meta_brain_lora_routing/artifacts/dream_reports/dream_20260515T154653/median/review_report.md`."}],"totalDurationMs":141819,"totalTokens":135211,"totalToolUseCount":20,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3451,"cache_read_input_tokens":131313,"output_tokens":446,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":3451},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":1,"output_tokens":446,"cache_read_input_tokens":131313,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3451,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":3451,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"toolStats":{"readCount":8,"searchCount":3,"bashCount":2,"editFileCount":0,"linesAdded":0,"linesRemoved":0,"otherToolCount":7}}}
